{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VXTB6GM9nRqDawzaNNTaEz","type":"tool_result","content":"# Working in this repo\n\n## Finish every change on main\n\n- When a `/goal` is complete, or a prompt has changed the repo, commit and\n  push to `origin/main` right away.\n- Pushing does not deploy. Vercel usage costs too much to build every\n  change, so Git deploys are off (`\"git\": { \"deploymentEnabled\": false }`\n  in `vercel.json`) and the site runs locally: `pnpm dev`, then\n  http://127.0.0.1:7417. Deploy to Vercel only when Michael explicitly asks,\n  for a major update: push with `deploymentEnabled` set to `true` (that push\n  deploys; check it reaches READY), then set it back to `false` in the next\n  commit, which does not deploy.\n- Work on `main`. If a branch is ever needed, merge it into main and delete\n  it (locally and on GitHub) in the same session. Never leave a local\n  branch, an unpushed commit, a stash, or an open PR behind.\n- Before starting work, run `git fetch --prune` and look at\n  `gh pr list`. Anything open gets resolved first.\n\n## Pull requests from others\n\nDecide each one; do not let it sit. Accept it (merge to main, delete the\nbranch), reject it (close it with a one-line reason), or replace it (close\nit, and land a better version on main that says which PR it replaces).\n\n## Keep it simple and clean\n\n- No dependencies, no build step, no generated files committed\n  (`data/games.json` is gitignored and rebuilt by `scripts/scan.mjs`).\n- Run `pnpm test` (or `node --test \"scripts/**/*.test.mjs\"`) before\n  committing code.\n- Delete what is no longer used instead of leaving it around.\n\n## When something goes wrong\n\nRoll back rather than leave half-finished work. Revert the commit\n(`git revert`) or restore the last good state and push that, so main is\nalways a working wall. Say what was rolled back and why.\n======\n196:in the Couch, with its own screenshots and URL for comparison. Its genre and\n242:pnpm test         # parsers, layout rules, zip reading, search and filters, Couch and Catalogue logic\n267:If a game misbehaves in a frame, *Open on its own page* in its Details drawer\n287:Players is *Single player* or *Multiplayer*, and Multiplayer opens head counts\n315:(**Wall · Friends · Couch · Catalogue · Atlas · Timeline · Deck**) leads to six more, built over the same games\n323:friends**, to the Friends view. Every game that plays in a session says so\n326:record), on the Couch's hero and game page, and on the Deck's card. Each of\n333:- **The party.** *Host a game night* (Google sign-in, then the session's\n336:  session on this computer*, in up to four tabs with the hub's practice games.\n337:- **Made for game night**: the games built for sessions by hand (Blaze Cup,\n341:- **How a session works**, in three steps, and the **ways to win**.\n342:- **Games to play together**: every game that plays in a session, filed by\n344:  ghosts* (ghost), *Same start, side by side* (parallel) — and *Couch co-op*,\n347:  it plays, a session round's length and a search; each choice shows how\n352:  game* (a session that opens with it, then deals the rest), *Try it on this\n353:  computer*, and *Practise alone* in the hub's player. A couch co-op game has\n356:### The Couch — `/couch`\n362:*Play with friends* (the games that play in a session), one per genre, one for\n364:model that made three or more, *Originals*, *Couch co-op* (several players on\n374:| With friends (a game that plays in a session) | P | the hero's button |\n386:While a game runs the Couch claims nothing, keys and buttons alike. With no\n414:the whole library ghosted behind your selection, and clicking a bar adds its\n422:record, **F** favourites, **O** opens a game on its own page, **/** writes a\n462:## Playing together: AI Hub sessions\n465:through an **AI Hub session**: the hub deals the games (Random Mode), keeps\n469:What a game must do is the **AI Hub Session Protocol**, specified in\n480:  and it is how the existing library joins sessions.\n481:- **Ghost**: parallel, and each copy also shows the other players'\n486:Games tagged with the older modes keep working: `race` plays as ghost, `co-op`\n489:In short: the `hub:session` metas in the head, the small `session.js` client\n491:awards, and outside a session the game plays exactly as it always would. What\n494:[`docs/session-hub.md`](docs/session-hub.md). The plan behind all of it, and\n495:why, is [`docs/multiplayer-plan.md`](docs/multiplayer-plan.md).\n497:A game that declares it shows a *Hub session* line in its details\n499:with `has:session`. Those fields never become rails. A parallel game is\n500:not a multiplayer game on the wall: each player plays alone.\n502:Games that play in sessions include **Blaze Cup** (a shared world, in teams),\n504:Switchyard** (tagged race, so played as ghost), and **Grand Theft Motto III**\n516:checks with Playwright: a parallel game at 1 and 2 players, a ghost game or a\n518:each with a player leaving, then the game on its own. `--record` writes the\n519:verdict into `data/overrides.json`, where a failing game gets `\"session\": \"0\"`\n521:parallel; **Comet Dash**, ghost; **Star Arena**, a shared world) are the hub's\n525:### Bringing the library to sessions\n557:- A model, cheapest first, wires the score, the end and the session steps from\n564:  on its own compared with the original.\n568:  exactly as it was, with a `sessionNote` in `data/overrides.json` saying why,\n576:### A session — `/session`\n578:The session itself: players pick a generated name, take one of four seats,\n587:it does. A session hosted from a game's page in the Friends view\n588:(`/session?first=<slug>`) opens with that game on the list; the address drops\n589:it once the session has it. Everyone sees the list, and the next game's card\n592:After the picks, **Random Mode** deals. The hub deals every game that declares `hub:session` and\n593:seats everyone, in an order fixed by the session's seed, and none comes round\n596:Ghost, Shared world), by round length (Short, Medium, Long), by genre, and by\n608:screen crowns the winner with a podium and the session awards (Showstopper,\n612:**Across devices** (`/session`):\n614:  `/session#<code>`.\n618:  of the session.\n624:- While no game in the library declares `hub:session`, the reference games\n625:  are dealt instead, so a session always has something to play.\n629:- A session nobody ended is ended after a day without activity (an hourly\n630:  job, `supabase/migrations/0005_end_stale_sessions.sql`).\n633:- Presence, round control and the WebRTC handshake go over the session's\n636:  `assets/js/session/mesh.js`), so a busy game costs the free plan nothing.\n647:http://localhost:7417/session?transport=local&examples=1#try      (open it in up to four tabs)\n654:- `node scripts/session-browser.mjs` plays a whole session in four tabs: a\n667:- hosting a session.\n694:  user's own votes, plays and sessions, and Google's tokens are not kept.\n750:| `players` | `1–2`, `1–4`… only when a game has co-op or versus | the Players rail: *Single player*, or *Multiplayer*, which drops a menu of head counts (*4 players* finds every game that seats four). A game with no `players` is single player |\n800:couch/            the Couch: a page of its own, over the same library","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"19307802-7215-43fb-a84b-6c94bbc636c5","uuid":"2368f77e-4ea9-40bf-b58b-52f46d2ace20","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:21:02.720Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# Working in this repo\n\n## Finish every change on main\n\n- When a `/goal` is complete, or a prompt has changed the repo, commit and\n  push to `origin/main` right away.\n- Pushing does not deploy. Vercel usage costs too much to build every\n  change, so Git deploys are off (`\"git\": { \"deploymentEnabled\": false }`\n  in `vercel.json`) and the site runs locally: `pnpm dev`, then\n  http://127.0.0.1:7417. Deploy to Vercel only when