{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FNReRM8vYmFUdt9HMaMqmS","type":"tool_result","content":"6: * hub:session-players allows: hello, ready under the hub's card with no key\n8: * once more with the host leaving. Then the game on its own, outside a session:\n9: * it opens, Enter and Space are pressed, and it must draw its screen with no\n29: * original page already had are forgiven when it is opened on its own.\n30: * --draws-only does only that last part, for any page: the retrofit runs it on\n34: * nothing with WebGL or a 2D canvas instead. --browser-args passes flags to\n37: *   --browser-args \"--enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-vulkan=swiftshader --use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader --use-angle=swiftshader\"\n44: * (it overrides the game's own hub:session meta, so Random Mode never deals\n47: * Usage:  node scripts/hub-check.mjs [game paths…] [--players 2,3,4] [--base URL] [--json] [--no-solo]\n48: *                                    [--retrofit [--original <path>]] [--draws-only] [--record] [--browser-args \"<flags>\"]\n66:const args = process.argv.slice(2);\n68:  const at = args.indexOf(`--${name}`);\n70:  const [value] = args.splice(at, 2).slice(1);\n76:const asJson = args.includes('--json');\n77:const solo = !args.includes('--no-solo');\n78:const retrofit = args.includes('--retrofit');\n79:const drawsOnly = args.includes('--draws-only');\n80:const record = args.includes('--record');\n82:const browserArgs = (option('browser-args', '') || '').split(/\\s+/).filter(Boolean);\n84:const games = args.filter((a) => !a.startsWith('--')).map(asPath);\n101:    const [least = 1, most = least] = (meta('hub:session-players')?.match(/\\d+/g) ?? []).map(Number);\n102:    return { mode: modeOf(meta('hub:session-mode')), seats: [least, most] };\n122:  // no WebGL drawing instead, means this browser cannot run it (a title screen may still show).\n174:const browser = await chromium.launch({ headless: true, executablePath: process.env.CHROMIUM_PATH, args: ['--no-sandbox', '--autoplay-policy=no-user-gesture-required', ...browserArgs] });\n178:    if (drawsOnly) {\n180:      runs.push({ game, players: 1, scenario: 'draws', pass: report.pass, checks: report.checks });\n181:      if (!asJson) console.log(`${report.pass ? 'PASS' : 'FAIL'}  ${game}  draws on its own`);\n210:      const finished = await page.waitForSelector('body[data-complete=\"true\"]', { timeout: PAGE_MS }).then(() => true, () => false);\n229:    if (solo) {\n233:        console.log(`${report.pass ? 'PASS' : 'FAIL'}  ${game}  on its own`);\n266: * The game on its own: open it as someone at the wall would, press Enter and\n267: * Space a few times, and see that it still runs: no errors (none beyond what\n269: * alone, and something drawn on the screen.\n281:    await tab.waitForTimeout(2500);\n282:    for (const key of ['Enter', 'Space', 'Enter', 'Space']) {\n284:      await tab.waitForTimeout(500);\n286:    await tab.waitForTimeout(2000);\n289:    // A WebGL or WebGPU canvas often reads back blank from a script, so look at the screen instead:\n290:    // a blank one compresses to almost nothing, so a PNG past a blank page's size means something is drawn.\n291:    const bytes = (await tab.screenshot({ type: 'png' }).catch(() => Buffer.alloc(0))).length;\n295:  const blank = await (async () => {\n299:    const bytes = (await tab.screenshot({ type: 'png' })).length;\n305:  after.drawn = after.bytes > blank + 1200;\n309:    check('on its own: the session client is there and inactive', after.hub && after.hub.active === false, JSON.stringify(after.hub));\n311:    check('on its own: Math.random is left alone', after.hub && after.hub.seeded !== true, JSON.stringify(after.hub));\n316:  check('on its own: this browser can run it', !noWebGPU, noWebGPU ? `it asked for WebGPU, this browser has no adapter, and drew nothing with WebGL or 2D instead (${asked})` : asked);\n317:  check('on its own: it draws its screen', after.drawn, `${after.bytes} bytes of screenshot, a blank screen is ${blank}`);\n319:  if (!bare) check(`on its own: no errors${before ? ' the original did not have' : ''}`, !fresh.length, fresh.slice(0, 3).join('; '));\n....\n|---|---|\n| 0 Watch | Parallel and ghost: the live scoreboard (*Now*). Shared worlds: a copy with no player of its own, fed the same traffic (*Later*) |\n| 1 Parallel | Mode `parallel`, client 1.3.0 (*Now*) |\n| 2 Ghosts | Mode `ghost`: parallel, plus the other players shown while they are in the same area, never touching a world (`race` until Nov 2) |\n| 3 Together | Mode `shared-world`: the host's copy runs the world (`versus` and `co-op` until Nov 2) |\n| 4 Natural multiplayer | A shared world, in whatever form the game's own multiplayer takes |\n| 5 Couch and remote couch | Couch co-op on one screen stays each game's own (up to four controllers), unchanged. Remote couch co-op is **pinned**: friends far away would need the host's screen streamed to them as video |\n\n**One mode per game.** A list of modes per game would mean a code path and a\nconformance run per mode in every game, for a choice the hub never needs to\nmake. The lobby needs no new picker either: the deal alternates between the\n- **Attract mode after 10 s idle** on the title screen: in a session there is\n  no title screen, so it never starts there. No conflict.\n- **Testing \"efficient\"**: the agent can still run the harness from the\n  protocol's *Test it*; the hub checks every game at import either way.\n- **Up to four players locally, controller first**: welcome. Couch co-op in\n  one room is the game's own; remote couch co-op is pinned.\n\nIf cc-matrix builds are imported, the hub's importer (`import-matrix-runs.mjs`,\nwritten for gpt-matrix's layout) needs to learn cc-matrix's `runs/<id>/work/`\n....\n489:In short: the `hub:session` metas in the head, the small `session.js` client\n592:After the picks, **Random Mode** deals. The hub deals every game that declares `hub:session` and\n623:  the browser, as `localStorage['ai-hub:relay-only']`).\n624:- While no game in the library declares `hub:session`, the reference games\n734:own, with `<meta name=\"hub:model\" content=\"…\">` in its head. A field whose\n741:an override, or a `hub:collection` meta, replaces it.\n757:checks. A game can name its own source with `<meta name=\"hub:source\">`\n758:(`hub:inspired-by`, the older name, still works). Source leads the rail strip.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"19307802-7215-43fb-a84b-6c94bbc636c5","uuid":"04931553-81ff-40cd-9f87-82e79b702f8a","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:21:29.275Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"6: * hub:session-players allows: hello, ready under the hub's card with no key\n8: * once more with the host leaving. Then the game on its own, outside a session:\n9: * it opens, Enter and Space are pressed, and it must draw its screen with no\n29: * original page already had are forgiven when it is opened on its own.\n30: * --draws-only does only that last part, for any page: the retrofit runs it on\n34: * nothing with WebGL or a 2D canvas instead. --browser-args passes flags to\n37: *   --browser-args \"--enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-vulkan=swiftshader --use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader --use-angle=swiftshader\"\n44: * (it overrides the game's own hub:session meta, so Random Mode never deals\n47: * Usage:  node scripts/hub-check.mjs [game paths…] [--players 2,3,4] [--base URL] [--json] [--no-solo]\n48: *                                    [--retrofit [--original <path>]] [--draws-only] [--record] [--browser-args \"<flags>\"]\n66:const args = process.argv.slice(2);\n68:  const at = args.indexOf(`--${name}`);\n70:  const [value] = args.splice(at, 2).slice(1);\n76:const asJson = args.includes('--json');\n77:const solo = !args.includes('--no-solo');\n78:const retrofit = args.includes('--retrofit');\n79:const drawsOnly = args.includes('--draws-only');\n80:const record = args.includes('--record');\n82:const b