{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjCfb9AkZvBBm93br19a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The flail works as a last-moment save at about 30°, holding 3 N·m, so I'm correcting the plan now, including my earlier overstatement about the gravity-tilt island.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3178,"cache_read_input_tokens":388119,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3178},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"19307802-7215-43fb-a84b-6c94bbc636c5","uuid":"445697cf-a250-4d1f-9ccb-e6609412044c","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:08:21.630Z","request_id":"req_011CgjCfar4fX6h5Pt15Ccje","narration_block_indexes":[0],"thinking_duration_ms":1,"thinking_display":"updates"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjCfb9AkZvBBm93br19a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012AB9jXw4ohnDGKDLDui8op","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211905__xe6f2a4/work && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='PLAN.md'\ns=open(p,encoding='utf-8').read()\ndef sub(old,new,count=1):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(old)>=1, 'MISSING: '+old[:70]\n    s=s.replace(old,new) if count==0 else s.replace(old,new,count)\n\n# section 2: avatar wording\nsub(\"No white-and-pale-blue gym, no plain white-clad instructor, no round-headed avatar with a big-eyed face, no talking board, no piggy bank.\",\n    \"No white-and-pale-blue gym, no plain white-clad instructor, no Mii-style avatars (ours are jointed wooden peg dolls), no talking board, no piggy bank.\")\n\n# section 3: cross on the island, disconnects\nsub(\"- **Create + Options belongs to the hub.** Ignore Options while Create (button 8) is held, everywhere.\",\n    \"- **On the island,** Cross and E use the focused thing if there is one; otherwise Cross and Space hop.\\n- **Create + Options belongs to the hub.** Ignore Options while Create (button 8) is held, everywhere.\\n- **If a player's pad disconnects mid-class,** pause and say so on screen.\")\n\n# section 4: what the numbers do\na=s.index(\"**What those numbers do ✔:**\")\nb=s.index(\"**The load rule ✔.**\")\ns=s[:a]+\"\"\"**What those numbers do ✔:**\n- Full stick from rest reaches 90% in about 1 s, overshoots to about 23° and settles at 18°. It is a soft, wobbly, toy-like feel.\n- Whipping the stick end to end at about 0.5 Hz survives. Slamming it from −18° to +18° peaks near 28° at `ankleMax` 4.2 and up, and falls at 3.8. This is why careful correction matters.\n- The torque limit makes a natural point of no return at `asin(ankleMax / G)`, about 39° with no load. Hat and stone loads lower it automatically.\n\n**Gusts at the defaults ✔ (0.5 s long; these numbers are the difficulty dial):**\n\n| Gust | Do nothing | Flail as you pass about 30° | Stick against it once it has started | Braced: stick at 60% against it, 0.5 s before it hits |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 2 N·m | safe, peaks 22° | | | |\n| 2.5 N·m | safe, peaks 31° | | | |\n| 3 N·m | **falls** | saved, peaks 38° | falls | safe, peaks 19° |\n| 3.5 N·m | falls | saved only if timed near 32°, peaks 43° | falls | safe, peaks 29° |\n| 4 N·m | falls | falls | falls | falls |\n\nSo a telegraph is worth a lot: **give a warning before every gust of 3 N·m or more.** And flail is a real last-moment save with timing in it: a flail used early, before you have moved much, wears off and you still fall. It is the moment people will shout at the TV.\n\n\"\"\"+s[b:]\n\nsub(\"Too heavy and the doll tips over at once: with margin 0.45, a 0.06 kg fruit tips it at the 5th catch, a 0.015 kg fruit around the 12th. **Keep prop masses small** (0.01 to 0.03 kg) against the doll's 1 kg.\",\n    \"Too heavy and the doll tips over at once: with margin 0.45, 0.06 kg fruit tipped it at the 5th or 6th catch, while 0.015 kg works out to about 13. **Keep prop masses small** (0.01 to 0.03 kg) against the doll's 1 kg.\")\nsub(\"Sway units are N·m. Sway near 0.2 moves the dot a third of the disc if ignored. Tremor is mostly for looks and rumble.\",\n    \"Sway units are N·m. Sway of 0.2 moves the dot about a quarter of the disc if ignored. Tremor is mostly for looks and rumble.\")\nsub(\"- **No physical step bob.** A kinematic foot bobbing 3 cm at walking pace throws everything off a tray. Bob the visual only. Ramp foot speed up over 1.5 s.\",\n    \"- **No physical step bob.** With a kinematic foot bobbing 3 cm at walking pace, everything left the tray within 20 s. Bob the visual only. Ramp foot speed up over 1.5 s.\")\nsub(\"**Flail.** One button, all devices. Arms windmill for 0.35 s and the ankle gets `flailBoost` strength. Cooldown is 2 s. It looks ridiculous on purpose. It is the save that makes near-falls exciting.\",\n    \"**Flail.** One button, all devices. Arms windmill for 0.35 s and the ankle gets `flailBoost` strength. Cooldown is 2 s. It looks ridiculous on purpose. It is the save that makes near-falls exciting, and it only works if you time it (see the table above).\")\n\n# section 5\nsub(\"| 5 | Level Day | Best-of-three | Tippy Raft, Tug of Peace, The Grand Hold | The ending |\",\"| 5 | Level Day | Your three best tests | Tippy Raft, Tug of Peace, The Grand Hold | The ending |\")\nsub(\"**Medals** come from form (0 to 100): ≥40 Adequate, ≥65 Pleasant, ≥85 Exemplary, ≥97 Suspicious. Below 40 is still a pass (\\\"Attended\\\"). Each event sets its own `par` so that form = 100 × raw/par. Set `par` per tier so the sharp bot lands 88 to 95 (section 17).\",\n    \"**Medals** come from form (0 to 100): ≥40 Adequate, ≥65 Pleasant, ≥85 Exemplary, ≥97 Suspicious. Below 40 is still a pass (\\\"Attended\\\"). Events that measure a share of the maximum (Poses, Still Water) use it directly. All others set a `par` so that form = 100 × raw/par, per tier, so the sharp bot lands 88 to 95 (section 17).\")\nsub(\"The programme uses Tier 1, except Day 5 and later use the highest tier opened. Free Play offers all open tiers.\",\n    \"Days 1 to 5 use Tier 1. Maintenance days use the highest tier opened. Free Play offers all open tiers.\")\n\n# section 6: cairn\nsub(\"Release 1.2 cm above the current top stone's centre with a small random offset.\",\"Release each stone 1.2 cm above the current top stone's centre with a small random offset.\")\nsub(\"- *Tiers ✔:* Tier 1: 6 stones every 5.5 s, hold 8 s, sway .1→.3, tremor .05→.15, offset 3 cm. Everyone finishes this one with the stack up: it teaches. Tier 2: 8 stones every 5 s, hold 10 s, sway .15→.4, tremor .08→.2, offset 4 cm: the stack sometimes goes at the 8th stone. Tier 3: 10 stones every 4.5 s, hold 10 s, sway .2→.45, tremor .1→.2, offset 5 cm: expect collapses around stones 8-9 without breath sync.\",\n    \"- *Tiers ✔ (without breath sync):* Tier 1: 6 stones every 5.5 s, hold 8 s, sway .1→.3, tremor .05→.15, offset ±1.5 cm. Every bot finished with all six up: it teaches. Tier 2: 8 stones every 5 s, hold 10 s, sway .15→.4, tremor .08→.2, offset ±2 cm: the stack sometimes goes at the 8th stone, clumsy players lose it more often. Tier 3: 10 stones every 4.5 s, hold 10 s, sway .2→.55, tremor .1→.25, offset ±2.5 cm: every bot collapsed around stones 7-9 and ended with 2-5 left. It is called Unreasonable for a reason, and breath sync is the way through.\")\n\n# log\nsub(\"- *Physics ✔:* Log: cylinder half-length .75, radius .09, mass .06, friction .2, on saddle colliders with friction .15. It slides about 0.1 m at 20° of lean and stays on.\",\n    \"- *Physics ✔:* margin .8. Log: cylinder half-length .75, radius .09, mass .06, friction .2, on saddle colliders with friction .15. It slides about 0.1 m at 20° of lean and stays on.\")\n\n# step class windows\nsub(\"- *Windows ✔ untested, starting:* Perfect ±45 ms, Good ±90, OK ±135.\",\"- *Windows (starting values):* Perfect ±45 ms, Good ±90, OK ±135.\")\n\n# room service\nsub(\"- *Physics ✔:* margin .8. Tray: cuboid (.3, .02, .3) at local (0, .5, .3), mass .04, friction 1, on the doll's body. Tumblers: cylinder half-height .06, radius .05, mass .012, friction .9, restitution 0, angular damping .5, linear damping .1. **At 1.2 m/s they hold through ±6° of sway, start to go at ±10-14°, and spill at ±20°.** Rims make little difference. Tall glasses (half-height .08+) fall over at walking pace: do not use them.\",\n    \"- *Physics ✔:* margin .8, ankleMax 6. Tray: cuboid (.3, .02, .3) at local (0, .5, .3), mass .04, friction 1, on the doll's body. Five tumblers: cylinder half-height .06, radius .05, mass .012, friction .9, restitution 0, angular damping .5, linear damping .1. **Walking at 1.2 m/s for 20 s, all five stayed on through ±14° of steady sway, and ±20° lost two.** A rim on the tray made little difference. Sudden gusts and falls are what cost glasses.\")\nsub(\"- *Tiers:* 30, 45, 60 m. Stride .55 m in .35 s. Gusts 2, 2.6, 3 N·m.\",\"- *Tiers:* 30, 45, 60 m. Stride .55 m in .35 s. Gusts 2, 2.6, 3 N·m, always telegraphed.\")\n\n# island\nsub(\"**Do not move the island. Tilt gravity.** Rapier sees a fixed flat disc; the visual island group rotates; gravity is set to match each step. This was far steadier than a kinematic platform: walker height stayed within 0.004 m against 0.17 m, with 60 props sliding to the low side and none lost.\",\n    \"**Do not move the island. Tilt gravity.** Rapier sees a fixed flat disc; the visual island group rotates; gravity is set to match each step. All the physics stays in island-local coordinates, with no moving-platform problems to solve. Up to 11° of tilt, a walker's height stayed within 0.004 m, and 60 props slid to the low side with none lost. (A kinematic platform also worked, but it is more to manage: I only took it to 1.8° and props rolled off.)\")\n\n# hub boot path\nsub(\"\"\"**The boot path** (first statements of `main.js`, before anything heavy):\n```js\nif (AIHub.active) {\n  const pConnect = AIHub.connect({ mode: 'ghost', seats: [1, 4], card: true });   // hello must go out within 10 s\n  await bootEngine();                       // renderer.init(), RAPIER.init(), build the world\n  const info = await pConnect;\n  if (info) runSession(info); else runStandalone();     // null: no hub after all\n} else { await bootEngine(); runStandalone(); }\n```\"\"\",\"\"\"**The boot path** (first statements of `main.js`, before anything heavy). Wrap it in an async function: an `iife` build rejects top-level `await`.\n```js\nasync function main() {\n  if (AIHub.active) {\n    const pConnect = AIHub.connect({ mode: 'ghost', seats: [1, 4], card: true });   // hello must go out within 10 s\n    await bootEngine();                       // renderer.init(), RAPIER.init(), build the world\n    const info = await pConnect;\n    if (info) runSession(info); else runStandalone();     // null: no hub after all\n  } else { await bootEngine(); runStandalone(); }\n}\nmain().catch(showBootFailure);                // shows the message, calls AIHub.fail(message)\n```\"\"\")\nsub(\"Triangle or M or a tap: `AIHub.answer('more')`.\",\"Triangle or M (name the key on the card) or a tap: `AIHub.answer('more')`.\")\nsub(\"4. **Ghosts.** About 10 times a second, `AIHub.send(\",\"4. **Ghosts.** From the moment `AIHub.time()` reaches 0, including during intros, about 10 times a second, `AIHub.send(\")\nsub(\"5. **Scoring.** Each slot gives `round(form × 10)`. `AIHub.progress({ score, label: 'Fruit Hat 420' })` every second during play.\",\n    \"5. **Scoring.** Each slot gives `round(form × 10)`. Call `AIHub.progress({ score, label: 'Fruit Hat 420' })` every second **from the moment time reaches 0, with score 0 during the first intro.** The harness checks for ghost traffic and progress about 4 seconds into play, well before the first class starts, and fails the game if there is none.\")\n\n# dev mode: designer tools wording\nsub(\"Tell yourself what \\\"designer tools\\\" means here: events, tiers, poses, charts, dialogue, days, unlocks, palettes and tuning are all plain data tables in `src/data/`. A designer can add an event's tier, a day or a line of dialogue without touching systems, and test it from Dev Mode. Keep it that way.\",\n    \"**For later designers.** TASK.md wants the rest of the game buildable with normal designer tools. So events' tiers, poses, charts, dialogue, days, unlocks, palettes and tuning are all plain data tables in `src/data/`. A designer can add a tier, a day or a line of dialogue without touching systems, and test it from Dev Mode. Keep it that way.\")\n\n# section 16\nsub(\"Expect 5-6 MB at the end.\",\"Expect about 4-6 MB at the end.\")\nsub(\"**Fresh world per event ✔.** Events get\",\"**Fresh world per event.** Events get\")\n\n# section 17: balance test wording\nsub(\"and parking the stick and doing nothing scores below 65 in Poses.\",\"and a bot that parks the stick exactly on the goal and never corrects stays below Exemplary in Poses (measured ✔ 75-81 on Tier 1).\")\nsub(\"*hub:* serve the built game plus `tools/hub/{harness.html,bridge.js,round.js}` from\",\"*hub:* fetch `harness.html`, `bridge.js` and `round.js` into `tools/hub/` from the same raw folder as the client. Serve the built game beside them from\")\nsub(\"The harness calls time after a few seconds, so `time-up` must work from any point.\",\"The harness calls time about 5 seconds into play, so `time-up` must work from any point, and a `result` with score 0 is valid.\")\nopen(p,'w',encoding='utf-8').write(s)\nprint('ok', len(s.split()), 'words')\nEOF\ngrep -n -iE \"GameTitle|exit-interview\\.json|claude-opus|claude-|20261104|planner-exit|\\.html\\]\" PLAN.md | head; echo \"--- ✔ count:\"; grep -c \"✔\" PLAN.md","description":"Apply review corrections to the plan and check for banned names"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3178,"cache_read_input_tokens":388119,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3178},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"19307802-7215-43fb-a84b-6c94bbc636c5","uuid":"da5d0665-fdeb-4e4f-9093-398dce301e4e","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:09:01.014Z","request_id":"req_011CgjCfar4fX6h5Pt15Ccje","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_012AB9jXw4ohnDGKDLDui8op":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211905__xe6f2a4/work && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='PLAN.md'\ns=open(p,encoding='utf-8').read()\ndef sub(old,new,count=1):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(old)>=1, 'MISSING: '+old[:70]\n    s=s.replace(old,new) if count==0 else s.replace(old,new,count)\n\n# section 2: avatar wording\nsub(\"No white-and-pale-blue gym, no plain white-clad instructor, no round-headed avatar with a big-eyed face, no talking board, no piggy bank.\",\n    \"No white-and-pale-blue gym, no plain white-clad instructor, no Mii-style avatars (ours are jointed wooden peg dolls), no talking board, no piggy bank.\")\n\n# section 3: cross on the island, disconnects\nsub(\"- **Create + Options belongs to the hub.** Ignore Options while Create (button 8) is held, everywhere.\",\n    \"- **On the island,** Cross and E use the focused thing if there is one; otherwise Cross and Space hop.\\n- **Create + Options belongs to the hub.** Ignore Options while Create (button 8) is held, everywhere.\\n- **If a player's pad disconnects mid-class,** pause and say so on screen.\")\n\n# section 4: what the numbers do\na=s.index(\"**What those numbers do ✔:**\")\nb=s.index(\"**The load rule ✔.**\")\ns=s[:a]+\"\"\"**What those numbers do ✔:**\n- Full stick from rest reaches 90% in about 1 s, overshoots to about 23° and settles at 18°. It is a soft, wobbly, toy-like feel.\n- Whipping the stick end to end at about 0.5 Hz survives. Slamming it from −18° to +18° peaks near 28° at `ankleMax` 4.2 and up, and falls at 3.8. This is why careful correction matters.\n- The torque limit makes a natural point of no return at `asin(ankleMax / G)`, about 39° with no load. Hat and stone loads lower it automatically.\n\n**Gusts at the defaults ✔ (0.5 s long; these numbers are the difficulty dial):**\n\n| Gust | Do nothing | Flail as you pass about 30° | Stick against it once it has started | Braced: stick at 60% against it, 0.5 s before it hits |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 2 N·m | safe, peaks 22° | | | |\n| 2.5 N·m | safe, peaks 31° | | | |\n| 3 N·m | **falls** | saved, peaks 38° | falls | safe, peaks 19° |\n| 3.5 N·m | falls | saved only if timed near 32°, peaks 43° | falls | safe, peaks 29° |\n| 4 N·m | falls | falls | falls | falls |\n\nSo a telegraph is worth a lot: **give a warning before every gust of 3 N·m or more.** And flail is a real last-moment save with timing in it: a flail used early, before you have moved much, wears off and you still fall. It is the moment people will shout at the TV.\n\n\"\"\"+s[b:]\n\nsub(\"Too heavy and the doll tips over at once: with margin 0.45, a 0.06 kg fruit tips it at the 5th catch, a 0.015 kg fruit around the 12th. **Keep prop masses small** (0.01 to 0.03 kg) against the doll's 1 kg.\",\n    \"Too heavy and the doll tips over at once: with margin 0.45, 0.06 kg fruit tipped it at the 5th or 6th catch, while 0.015 kg works out to about 13. **Keep prop masses small** (0.01 to 0.03 kg) against the doll's 1 kg.\")\nsub(\"Sway units are N·m. Sway near 0.2 moves the dot a third of the disc if ignored. Tremor is mostly for looks and rumble.\",\n    \"Sway units are N·m. Sway of 0.2 moves the dot about a quarter of the disc if ignored. Tremor is mostly for looks and rumble.\")\nsub(\"- **No physical step bob.** A kinematic foot bobbing 3 cm at walking pace throws everything off a tray. Bob the visual only. Ramp foot speed up over 1.5 s.\",\n    \"- **No physical step bob.** With a kinematic foot bobbing 3 cm at walking pace, everything left the tray within 20 s. Bob the visual only. Ramp foot speed up over 1.5 s.\")\nsub(\"**Flail.** One button, all devices. Arms windmill for 0.35 s and the ankle gets `flailBoost` strength. Cooldown is 2 s. It looks ridiculous on purpose. It is the save that makes near-falls exciting.\",\n    \"**Flail.** One button, all devices. Arms windmill for 0.35 s and the ankle gets `flailBoost` strength. Cooldown is 2 s. It looks ridiculous on purpose. It is the save that makes near-falls exciting, and it only works if you time it (see the table above).\")\n\n# section 5\nsub(\"| 5 | Level Day | Best-of-three | Tippy Raft, Tug of Peace, The Grand Hold | The ending |\",\"| 5 | Level Day | Your three best tests | Tippy Raft, Tug of Peace, The Grand Hold | The ending |\")\nsub(\"**Medals** come from form (0 to 100): ≥40 Adequate, ≥65 Pleasant, ≥85 Exemplary, ≥97 Suspicious. Below 40 is still a pass (\\\"Attended\\\"). Each event sets its own `par` so that form = 100 × raw/par. Set `par` per tier so the sharp bot lands 88 to 95 (section 17).\",\n    \"**Medals** come from form (0 to 100): ≥40 Adequate, ≥65 Pleasant, ≥85 Exemplary, ≥97 Suspicious. Below 40 is still a pass (\\\"Attended\\\"). Events that measure a share of the maximum (Poses, Still Water) use it directly. All others set a `par` so that form = 100 × raw/par, per tier, so the sharp bot lands 88 to 95 (section 17).\")\nsub(\"The programme uses Tier 1, except Day 5 and later use the highest tier opened. Free Play offers all open tiers.\",\n    \"Days 1 to 5 use Tier 1. Maintenance days use the highest tier opened. Free Play offers all open tiers.\")\n\n# section 6: cairn\nsub(\"Release 1.2 cm above the current top stone's centre with a small random offset.\",\"Release each stone 1.2 cm above the current top stone's centre with a small random offset.\")\nsub(\"- *Tiers ✔:* Tier 1: 6 stones every 5.5 s, hold 8 s, sway .1→.3, tremor .05→.15, offset 3 cm. Everyone finishes this one with the stack up: it teaches. Tier 2: 8 stones every 5 s, hold 10 s, sway .15→.4, tremor .08→.2, offset 4 cm: the stack sometimes goes at the 8th stone. Tier 3: 10 stones every 4.5 s, hold 10 s, sway .2→.45, tremor .1→.2, offset 5 cm: expect collapses around stones 8-9 without breath sync.\",\n    \"- *Tiers ✔ (without breath sync):* Tier 1: 6 stones every 5.5 s, hold 8 s, sway .1→.3, tremor .05→.15, offset ±1.5 cm. Every bot finished with all six up: it teaches. Tier 2: 8 stones every 5 s, hold 10 s, sway .15→.4, tremor .08→.2, offset ±2 cm: the stack sometimes goes at the 8th stone, clumsy players lose it more often. Tier 3: 10 stones every 4.5 s, hold 10 s, sway .2→.55, tremor .1→.25, offset ±2.5 cm: every bot collapsed around stones 7-9 and ended with 2-5 left. It is called Unreasonable for a reason, and breath sync is the way through.\")\n\n# log\nsub(\"- *Physics ✔:* Log: cylinder half-length .75, radius .09, mass .06, friction .2, on saddle colliders with friction .15. It slides about 0.1 m at 20° of lean and stays on.\",\n    \"- *Physics ✔:* margin .8. Log: cylinder half-length .75, radius .09, mass .06, friction .2, on saddle colliders with friction .15. It slides about 0.1 m at 20° of lean and stays on.\")\n\n# step class windows\nsub(\"- *Windows ✔ untested, starting:* Perfect ±45 ms, Good ±90, OK ±135.\",\"- *Windows (starting values):* Perfect ±45 ms, Good ±90, OK ±135.\")\n\n# room service\nsub(\"- *Physics ✔:* margin .8. Tray: cuboid (.3, .02, .3) at local (0, .5, .3), mass .04, friction 1, on the doll's body. Tumblers: cylinder half-height .06, radius .05, mass .012, friction .9, restitution 0, angular damping .5, linear damping .1. **At 1.2 m/s they hold through ±6° of sway, start to go at ±10-14°, and spill at ±20°.** Rims make little difference. Tall glasses (half-height .08+) fall over at walking pace: do not use them.\",\n    \"- *Physics ✔:* margin .8, ankleMax 6. Tray: cuboid (.3, .02, .3) at local (0, .5, .3), mass .04, friction 1, on the doll's body. Five tumblers: cylinder half-height .06, radius .05, mass .012, friction .9, restitution 0, angular damping .5, linear damping .1. **Walking at 1.2 m/s for 20 s, all five stayed on through ±14° of steady sway, and ±20° lost two.** A rim on the tray made little difference. Sudden gusts and falls are what cost glasses.\")\nsub(\"- *Tiers:* 30, 45, 60 m. Stride .55 m in .35 s. Gusts 2, 2.6, 3 N·m.\",\"- *Tiers:* 30, 45, 60 m. Stride .55 m in .35 s. Gusts 2, 2.6, 3 N·m, always telegraphed.\")\n\n# island\nsub(\"**Do not move the island. Tilt gravity.** Rapier sees a fixed flat disc; the visual island group rotates; gravity is set to match each step. This was far steadier than a kinematic platform: walker height stayed within 0.004 m against 0.17 m, with 60 props sliding to the low side and none lost.\",\n    \"**Do not move the island. Tilt gravity.** Rapier sees a fixed flat disc; the visual island group rotates; gravity is set to match each step. All the physics stays in island-local coordinates, with no moving-platform problems to solve. Up to 11° of tilt, a walker's height stayed within 0.004 m, and 60 props slid to the low side with none lost. (A kinematic platform also worked, but it is more to manage: I only took it to 1.8° and props rolled off.)\")\n\n# hub boot path\nsub(\"\"\"**The boot path** (first statements of `main.js`, before anything heavy):\n```js\nif (AIHub.active) {\n  const pConnect = AIHub.connect({ mode: 'ghost', seats: [1, 4], card: true });   // hello must go out within 10 s\n  await bootEngine();                       // renderer.init(), RAPIER.init(), build the world\n  const info = await pConnect;\n  if (info) runSession(info); else runStandalone();     // null: no hub after all\n} else { await bootEngine(); runStandalone(); }\n```\"\"\",\"\"\"**The boot path** (first statements of `main.js`, before anything heavy). Wrap it in an async function: an `iife` build rejects top-level `await`.\n```js\nasync function main() {\n  if (AIHub.active) {\n    const pConnect = AIHub.connect({ mode: 'ghost', seats: [1, 4], card: true });   // hello must go out within 10 s\n    await bootEngine();                       // renderer.init(), RAPIER.init(), build the world\n    const info = await pConnect;\n    if (info) runSession(info); else runStandalone();     // null: no hub after all\n  } else { await bootEngine(); runStandalone(); }\n}\nmain().catch(showBootFailure);                // shows the message, calls AIHub.fail(message)\n```\"\"\")\nsub(\"Triangle or M or a tap: `AIHub.answer('more')`.\",\"Triangle or M (name the key on the card) or a tap: `AIHub.answer('more')`.\")\nsub(\"4. **Ghosts.** About 10 times a second, `AIHub.send(\",\"4. **Ghosts.** From the moment `AIHub.time()` reaches 0, including during intros, about 10 times a second, `AIHub.send(\")\nsub(\"5. **Scoring.** Each slot gives `round(form × 10)`. `AIHub.progress({ score, label: 'Fruit Hat 420' })` every second during play.\",\n    \"5. **Scoring.** Each slot gives `round(form × 10)`. Call `AIHub.progress({ score, label: 'Fruit Hat 420' })` every second **from the moment time reaches 0, with score 0 during the first intro.** The harness checks for ghost traffic and progress about 4 seconds into play, well before the first class starts, and fails the game if there is none.\")\n\n# dev mode: designer tools wording\nsub(\"Tell yourself what \\\"designer tools\\\" means here: events, tiers, poses, charts, dialogue, days, unlocks, palettes and tuning are all plain data tables in `src/data/`. A designer can add an event's tier, a day or a line of dialogue without touching systems, and test it from Dev Mode. Keep it that way.\",\n    \"**For later designers.** TASK.md wants the rest of the game buildable with normal designer tools. So events' tiers, poses, charts, dialogue, days, unlocks, palettes and tuning are all plain data tables in `src/data/`. A designer can add a tier, a day or a line of dialogue without touching systems, and test it from Dev Mode. Keep it that way.\")\n\n# section 16\nsub(\"Expect 5-6 MB at the end.\",\"Expect about 4-6 MB at the end.\")\nsub(\"**Fresh world per event ✔.** Events get\",\"**Fresh world per event.** Events get\")\n\n# section 17: balance test wording\nsub(\"and parking the stick and doing nothing scores below 65 in Poses.\",\"and a bot that parks the stick exactly on the goal and never corrects stays below Exemplary in Poses (measured ✔ 75-81 on Tier 1).\")\nsub(\"*hub:* serve the built game plus `tools/hub/{harness.html,bridge.js,round.js}` from\",\"*hub:* fetch `harness.html`, `bridge.js` and `round.js` into `tools/hub/` from the same raw folder as the client. Serve the built game beside them from\")\nsub(\"The harness calls time after a few seconds, so `time-up` must work from any point.\",\"The harness calls time about 5 seconds into play, so `time-up` must work from any point, and a `result` with score 0 is valid.\")\nopen(p,'w',encoding='utf-8').write(s)\nprint('ok', len(s.split()), 'words')\nEOF\ngrep -n -iE \"GameTitle|exit-interview\\.json|claude-opus|claude-|20261104|planner-exit|\\.html\\]\" PLAN.md | head; echo \"--- ✔ count:\"; grep -c \"✔\" PLAN.md","description":"Apply review corrections to the plan and check for banned names"}}}
