{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjCo1wdMdwKNgrHSF3w5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The read-through turned up four gaps: Pause, Settings and Dev Mode break the six-choice rule, there's no rule for picking the stick, keys or pointer for weight, the jar and gull lack recipes, and a fall in Fruit Hat leaves the fruit's fate unstated. I'm fixing those and then reading the final stretch.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":17689,"cache_read_input_tokens":418878,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":17689},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"19307802-7215-43fb-a84b-6c94bbc636c5","uuid":"bae75c4c-c325-4f07-b17f-bf2d91d6f75b","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:10:03.723Z","request_id":"req_011CgjCo1eWuS1nnX3tvbKGy","narration_block_indexes":[0],"thinking_duration_ms":1,"thinking_display":"updates"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjCo1wdMdwKNgrHSF3w5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019iPhQ6xVzQHoptnYFNMuwc","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='PLAN.md'\ns=open(p,encoding='utf-8').read()\ndef sub(old,new):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(old)==1, ('COUNT %d: '%s.count(old))+old[:70]\n    s=s.replace(old,new)\n\nsub(\"- **Never use** the source's name (outside the title's joke and the About screen's Source line), its product or feature names\",\n    \"- **Never show** the source's name on screen (outside the title's joke and the About screen's Source line), nor use its product or feature names\")\n\n# weight source arbitration, cursor\nsub(\"- **No pointer lock is needed**, which keeps the game simple inside the hub's frames.\",\n    \"- **No pointer lock is needed**, which keeps the game simple inside the hub's frames. Hide the cursor during events when the mouse is in use: the faint ring on the Balance Disc shows where it is asking you to go.\\n- **Which device moves your weight:** whichever was used last. With a pad, ignore the pointer. With keyboard and mouse, keys win while a weight key is down, otherwise the pointer, once it has moved. A resting mouse never fights a resting stick.\")\n\n# disc as svg\nsub(\"**The Balance Disc.** `cob = (leanX, leanZ) / maxLean` is the dot, shown truthfully. It is the game's signature HUD:\",\n    \"**The Balance Disc.** `cob = (leanX, leanZ) / maxLean` is the dot, shown truthfully. Draw it as inline SVG and move it with transforms each frame. It is the game's signature HUD:\")\n\n# palettes pin\nsub(\"Palettes follow the day's steps (dawn, noon, golden, dusk).\",\"Palettes follow the day's steps (dawn, noon, golden, dusk), unless an event pins its own (Step Class at dusk, The Grand Hold at sunset).\")\n\n# fruit hat fall\nsub(\"Spiky urchins knock the basket and cost points. Old boots are heavy. A golden pineapple is worth five and very heavy. Flail shakes off whatever is on top.\",\n    \"A fall spills everything unbanked. Spiky urchins knock the basket and cost points. Old boots are heavy. A golden pineapple is worth five and very heavy. Flail shakes off whatever is on top.\")\n\n# raft gain\nsub(\"using the island's model (below) at a stronger gain, so everyone is on the same seesaw.\",\"using the island's model (below) at a stronger gain (start at 14° for one doll at the rim), so everyone is on the same seesaw.\")\n\n# island horizon sentence\nsub(\"- Only the island's visual tilts in the sky's frame: the sea and horizon stay level. The horizon against the crooked lighthouse is what sells it.\",\n    \"- The sea and horizon stay level; only the island tilts. The level horizon against the crooked lighthouse is what sells it.\")\n\n# screens: six-choice rule, pause, settings\nsub(\"At most six choices on a screen. One idea per screen.\",\"At most six choices on a screen, not counting a page switcher. Longer lists are split into pages. One idea per screen.\")\nsub(\"| Pause | Resume, Restart, How to Play, Settings, Dev Mode, About, Leave Class (to island). Stops the sim |\",\n    \"| Pause | Resume, Restart, How to Play, Settings, Dev Mode, Leave Class (to island). Stops the sim |\")\nsub(\"| Settings | Music (default **10**), Sound, Voice, glyph style, rumble, difficulty, auto-breathe, rhythm offset, UI scale, ink strength, reduce shake, fullscreen, reset save (with confirm). All sliders move with left and right, drag with mouse |\",\n    \"| Settings | Four pages. Sound: Music (default **10**), Sound, Voice. Controls: glyph style, rumble, auto-breathe, rhythm offset. Display: UI scale, ink strength, reduce shake, fullscreen. Game: difficulty, reset save (with an in-game confirm). Sliders move with left and right, drag with mouse |\")\nsub(\"| Main menu | Programme (or Continue), Group Class, Free Play, Journal, Settings, About |\",\"| Main menu | Programme (or Continue), Group Class, Free Play, Journal, Settings, About/Credits |\")\n\n# dev mode paged\nsub(\"From the Pause menu. It is one screen with big controls, usable by pad, keyboard and mouse.\",\n    \"From the Pause menu. It follows the same 10-foot rules: pages of big controls by group, six to a page, usable by pad, keyboard and mouse. Dev Mode is off in a session.\")\n\n# models: jar and gull\nsub(\"- **Island.** Sand disc r 22 over\",\n    \"- **Gary the gull.** White ellipsoid body, grey flattened wings, yellow cone beak, orange peg legs, ink dot eyes and one permanently angry brow.\\n- **The jar ✔.** `LatheGeometry` through (.01,0) (1,.02) (1.08,.12) (1.08,1.9) (.86,2.2) (.86,2.45) (.95,2.5) with the glass material below. Marbles: `InstancedMesh` of toon spheres r .14 with `setColorAt`. Physics: a base cylinder and a ring of 16 cuboid walls.\\n- **Island.** Sand disc r 22 over\")\n# glass is above jar? phrase check\nsub(\"with the glass material below.\",\"with the glass material from the gotchas above.\")\nopen(p,'w',encoding='utf-8').write(s)\nprint('words',len(s.split()))\nEOF\n","description":"Fix contradictions and gaps found on the read-through"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":17689,"cache_read_input_tokens":418878,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":17689},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"19307802-7215-43fb-a84b-6c94bbc636c5","uuid":"d99610d0-5cd8-4afc-82f6-baddb7f0bdc9","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:10:19.087Z","request_id":"req_011CgjCo1eWuS1nnX3tvbKGy","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_019iPhQ6xVzQHoptnYFNMuwc":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211905__xe6f2a4/work && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='PL