{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjCo1wdMdwKNgrHSF3w5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TPNSSwArf6j189RFJdxmf4","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211905__xe6f2a4/work/PLAN.md","offset":698},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":17689,"cache_read_input_tokens":418878,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":17689},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"19307802-7215-43fb-a84b-6c94bbc636c5","uuid":"c6709255-7c71-46e0-a9b0-c62d216bb32b","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:10:20.657Z","request_id":"req_011CgjCo1eWuS1nnX3tvbKGy","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01TPNSSwArf6j189RFJdxmf4":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211905__xe6f2a4/work/PLAN.md","offset":698}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TPNSSwArf6j189RFJdxmf4","type":"tool_result","content":"698\t\n699\t**Test hooks.** With `?test=1`, the game exposes `window.__TEST__`:\n700\t- `state()`: JSON with `screen, attract, day, step, profile, marbles, tilt, wobbleAge, event: { id, tier, phase, t, score, lanes: [{ kind, leanX, leanZ, cob, fallen, form, props }] }, input: { lastDevice, glyphSet }, audio: { state, music, sfx, voice }, render: { backend, frames }, errors`.\n701\t- `advance(seconds)`: runs the fixed tick and the frame logic without rendering or waiting. All tests use it, except the ones checking real time and real frames.\n702\t- `bot(skill | null)`: `sharp`, `average`, `clumsy` play through the real input path: they write to the stubbed gamepad, not into the game's state.\n703\t- `goto(screen, args)`, `tuning`, `settings`.\n704\tWith `?render=0`, the game skips creating a renderer, which makes logic tests fast. Rapier and all game logic still run.\n705\t\n706\t**Input stubs.** Replace `navigator.getGamepads` with `add_init_script`/`addInitScript`, returning `{ connected: true, mapping: 'standard', axes: [...], buttons: [{ pressed, value }, ...], vibrationActuator: { playEffect() {} } }` from `window.__pads`. Use `page.keyboard` and `page.mouse` for the rest.\n707\t\n708\t**The bots ✔ (human model, already calibrated).** A delayed correction: the bot sees the dot `delay` seconds ago and sets `wish = goal + gain × (goal − dot) + noise × sin(...)`. sharp: delay .16, gain 1.4 (use .7 under stacks). average: delay .26, gain 1.0 (.55 under stacks), noise .03. clumsy: delay .38, gain .8 (.45), noise .07. Do not raise gain under heavy load: it oscillates and tips, which is a bot failure and not a game bug.\n709\t\n710\t**Tests to write.**\n711\t\n712\t*unit* (Node, no browser): Wobble Age mapping and bounds; marble payouts; tier unlock rules; programme table integrity (every id exists, days still work with a Tier B event removed); charts valid; tuning defaults inside min and max; dialogue ids all exist; save corrupt or old version is handled; rng repeatable; the session client hash; the built HTML has the metas in `name`, `content` order, the client directly after `<meta charset>`, and no `</script` inside a script. **Source greps:** no `Math.random` outside `src/core/rng.js`; no `TODO`, `FIXME`, `placeholder`, `stub`; no `alert(`, `confirm(`, `prompt(`, `window.open`, `WebSocket`, `RTCPeerConnection`; no audio file extensions or `decodeAudioData`; none of the source's names (`/wii|mii\\b|balance board/i`) outside the title constant and `src/data/about.js`; no compute nodes.\n713\t\n714\t*flow:* **the scripted whole-game playthrough.** From a fresh save on `?test=1&render=0`: Title → profile → tutorial → all days through the real menus with a stubbed pad and the bot in every class → ending → credits → Maintenance day → Free Play has everything. Assert days, stamps, marbles rising, tilt falling to exactly 0, music detune reaching 0. Reload mid-way and assert the save resumes. Also attract: `advance(10)` on Title starts it, it visits at least four events, a key exits it and that key isn't acted on, and one wall-clock run of 10 real seconds. Also pause and resume, restart, Dev Mode opens only from Pause.\n715\t\n716\t*events:* for each event and tier, with the sharp bot: it completes, the result is valid, no NaN in any body, bodies return to the baseline count after `dispose()`, a forced fall ragdolls and recovers. One run with rendering on for each event for 2 s with `WEBGPU` flags: `backend === 'webgpu'`, frames rising, no console errors. One WebKit boot through a few events: WebGL2 backend, no errors.\n717\t\n718\t*balance:* run bots over 3 seeds per event at Tier 1 and assert: sharp reaches Exemplary (≥85) on average, average reaches Pleasant or Adequate, clumsy reaches at least Adequate (≥40), and a bot that parks the stick exactly on the goal and never corrects stays below Exemplary in Poses (measured ✔ 75-81 on Tier 1). Fruit Hat Tier 1: sharp banking at 7 has no falls and never banking has at least one. Use this test to set each `par`. This is how the plan's \"balance is key\" gets checked without a human.\n719\t\n720\t*input:* every verb from the pad stub, from keys, from the mouse, same game effect. Prompts switch the same frame (read `data-glyph`). Xbox glyph option. Menus fully navigable by pad alone, by keyboard alone, by mouse alone. Hover moves the focus. Clicks activate. Options ignored while Create is held. Four pads join Group Class, each controls its own lane. Tippy Raft has a winner.\n721\t\n722\t*audio:* music setting defaults to 10 and the bus gain is 0.10. Render each track, sting, SFX and voice with `OfflineAudioContext`: finite, non-silent (RMS above a floor), not clipped. Check detune at tilt 0 is zero.\n723\t\n724\t*hub:* fetch `harness.html`, `bridge.js` and `round.js` into `tools/hub/` from the same raw folder as the client. Serve the built game beside them from an in-process `http.createServer` on `listen(0, '127.0.0.1')`, so no port is hard-coded and no process needs stopping. First confirm the page is your game. Open `harness.html?game=GAME.html&players=N&auto=1` with `WEBGPU` plus `--no-sandbox --autoplay-policy=no-user-gesture-required`, wait for `body[data-complete=\"true\"]`, read `window.__hubCheck.pass` and print failing checks. Runs: `players=1`, `players=2`, `players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5`, and the same with `&scenario=host-leave`. Also on its own: open the page, press Enter, Space, Enter, Space, assert no errors, `AIHub.active` false and something drawn. The harness calls time about 5 seconds into play, so `time-up` must work from any point, and a `result` with score 0 is valid.\n725\t\n726\t*ui:* at 1920×1080, walk every screen and assert: no text under 30 px in computed style, nothing outside the viewport or the 5% margin except backgrounds, at most six focusable items, a visible focus. Touch-only: Pixel 7 and iPhone profiles show the message and Settings, tap opens Settings, no other controls respond, attract runs, a key or pad clears the state. About shows every Source Information field and the three feedback lists, and matches the exit-interview file.\n727\t\n728\t**Art pass, by eye, at the end.** `tools/shots.mjs` with `SHOTS` at 1920×1080: title, island on Day 1 and Day 5, each event mid-play, results, jar, Age Reveal, Group Class with four dolls, Dev Mode, About. Look for lost legibility at 10 feet, sunk characters, messy ink.\n729\t\n730\t---\n731\t\n732\t## 18. Build order and cut order\n733\t\n734\tEach milestone ends with something playable. Commit to the order: Fruit Hat before menus, because if the core isn't fun nothing else matters. Keep everything working as you go.\n735\t\n736\t| # | Milestone | Done when |\n737\t|---|---|---|\n738\t| 0 | Skeleton | Build script, single HTML, renderer with ink, sky and sea, Rapier, the loop, hooks, `test.mjs`, session client in place |\n739\t| 1 | The soul | Balance core, Balance Disc, doll with clips and ragdoll, input with all three devices, **Fruit Hat complete with results.** Tune until it makes you want one more go |\n740\t| 2 | The shell | Title, menu, Who's Here, island with tilt physics, Trudy with voice, dialogue, music engine, save, pause, settings, glyphs |\n741\t| 3 | The programme | Check-In, Wobble Age, Jar, Today's Plan, days. **Tier A events:** Poses, Log Reps, Step Class, The Cairn, Room Service, Plate Spinners, Springboard |\n742\t| 4 | The features | Attract, Dev Mode, Group Class, Tippy Raft, hub session, touch-only, About. Passing the hub harness |\n743\t| 5 | The ending | The Grand Hold, ending, credits, Maintenance days |\n744\t| 6 | Tier B events, in this order | Still Water, Plank & Perch, Tug of Peace, Island Loop |\n745\t| 7 | Polish | Juice, more lines, art pass, full tests, exit interview, final build |\n746\t\n747\t**Cut order if you run short. Cut whole things, never stub them, and leave no trace (TASK.md: no stubs, no placeholders).** First Island Loop, then Tug of Peace, then Plank & Perch, then Still Water, then Tier 3 of each event (leaving a two-tier ladder), then Tier 2. Do not cut: Fruit Hat, Poses, Check-In, Trudy, the tilting island, the jar, the finale, Attract, Dev Mode, Group Class, the hub session, glyphs, audio. The day table builds from the registry, so cutting an event needs no other change.\n748\t\n749\t---\n750\t\n751\t## 19. Done\n752\t\n753\tBefore you finish, check every line:\n754\t\n755\t- [ ] Single HTML where TASK.md says, opens from `file://`, no external requests, no audio files\n756\t- [ ] WebGPU backend by default, WebGL2 fallback works, ink filter on, Rapier 0.19.3, Three R180\n757\t- [ ] Original cast, events, art and music; title is your own random pick; nothing from section 2's lists\n758\t- [ ] All thirteen events, or the ones left after cuts, each with tiers, an intro, results and bots\n759\t- [ ] Programme through the ending, Wobble Age graph, jar, unlocks, Free Play\n760\t- [ ] Controller-first; keyboard and mouse native; prompts follow last device; Xbox glyph option; no dense screens\n761\t- [ ] Attract at 10 s, any input exits; Dev Mode from Pause with tools, live sliders and reset; touch-only message and Settings\n762\t- [ ] Group Class 1-4 on one screen; hub harness passes at 1, 2, 4 players, on the bad network, with the host leaving; game on its own passes Enter and Space\n763\t- [ ] Music at 10% by default; all sound in code; gibberish voices with every word on screen\n764\t- [ ] `node tools/test.mjs full` passes; a scripted whole-game playthrough is part of it\n765\t- [ ] No TODOs, placeholders or stubs in `src/`\n766\t- [ ] About/Credits has Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback, as TASK.md lists them, paged in large type\n767\t- [ ] The exit-interview file exists beside the HTML in TASK.md's exact shape, and parses\n768\t- [ ] Your chat reply has Source Information and all three feedback sections\n769\t\n770\t**About screen.** `tools/build.mjs` reads the exit-interview file into `src/data/about.js` so there's one source of truth. Write that file after your tests, rebuild, rerun `ui`. During development About shows what is known so far. Credit Fredoka (SIL OFL), Three.js and Rapier.\n771\t\n772\t**Filling in the exit interview.** Suggested: `type` Game, `genre` Sports, `source` Wii Fit, `series` empty (the franchise is the source itself, and the hub's catalogue wants it empty then), `players` 1–4, `tags` such as 3d, comedy, third-person, versus, arcade. `controls` can reuse the how-to line. Genre and perspective wording: section 1. Online: AI Hub Session Protocol v1 in ghost mode, 1-4 devices; plus 1-4 on one screen. Plan research (your own goes beside it): the hub's protocol pages and code; background on the source from Wikipedia, a Nintendo World Report review and Nintendo's Iwata Asks interviews, read as search summaries.\n773\t\n774\t---\n775\t\n776\t## 20. What was and wasn't verified\n777\t\n778\t**Tested here on 2026-11-04 (✔ above), with throwaway spikes:** versions exist on npm and jsDelivr; single-file esbuild build from `file://`; WebGPU in Chromium with SwiftShader; WebGL2 fallback in Chromium and WebKit; `toonOutlinePass` with MRT and the custom ink pass; instanced toon meshes and toon glass; shadow settings; the look of all characters and three palettes; the hub harness with WebGPU, own card and ghost mode; client hash; balance model; torque limit; gusts and flail; Fruit Hat as a full simulation with bots; Poses and The Cairn at all tiers with bots; tray and tumblers while walking; log on saddle; marble pours; ragdoll; tilted-gravity island; touch media queries; Fredoka's licence and file names.\n779\t\n780\t**Not tested. These are starting values, and they are your call:** Plate Spinners' bands, Step Class's windows, Springboard's numbers, Log Reps' ribbon, Plank's gull forces, Tug's power, Tippy Raft's gain, the noon palette, the walrus and heron animation. I could not listen to anything: the music is specified by theory, so check it with the audio tests and trust the arrangement. Nobody has played any of this with a real controller on a real TV.\n781\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"19307802-7215-43fb-a84b-6c94bbc636c5","uuid":"6d5d3f97-9bd5-471c-aa39-bd1157233175","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:10:20.663Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211905__xe6f2a4/work/PLAN.md","content":"\n**Test hooks.** With `?test=1`, the game exposes `window.__TEST__`:\n- `state()`: JSON with `screen, attract, day, step, profile, marbles, tilt, wobbleAge, event: { id, tier, phase, t, score, lanes: [{ kind, leanX, leanZ, cob, fallen, form, props }] }, input: { lastDevice, glyphSet }, audio: { state, music, sfx, voice }, render: { backend, frames }, errors`.\n- `advance(seconds)`: runs the fixed tick and the frame logic without rendering or waiting. All tests use it, except the ones checking real time and real frames.\n- `bot(skill | null)`: `sharp`, `average`, `clumsy` play through the real input path: they write to the stubbed gamepad, not into the game's state.\n- `goto(screen, args)`, `tuning`, `settings`.\nWith `?render=0`, the game skips creating a renderer, which makes logic tests fast. Rapier and all game logic still run.\n\n**Input stubs.** Replace `navigator.getGamepads` with `add_init_script`/`addInitScript`, returning `{ connected: true, mapping: 'standard', axes: [...], buttons: [{ pressed, value }, ...], vibrationActuator: { playEffect() {} } }` from `window.__pads`. Use `page.keyboard` and `page.mouse` for the rest.\n\n**The bots ✔ (human model, already calibrated).** A delayed correction: the bot sees the dot `delay` seconds ago and sets `wish = goal + gain × (goal − dot) + noise × sin(...)`. sharp: delay .16, gain 1.4 (use .7 under stacks). average: delay .26, gain 1.0 (.55 under stacks), noise .03. clumsy: delay .38, gain .8 (.45), noise .07. Do not raise gain under heavy load: it oscillates and tips, which is a bot failure and not a game bug.\n\n**Tests to write.**\n\n*unit* (Node, no browser): Wobble Age mapping and bounds; marble payouts; tier unlock rules; programme table integrity (every id exists, days still work with a Tier B event removed); charts valid; tuning defaults inside min and max; dialogue ids all exist; save corrupt or old version is handled; rng repeatable; the session client hash; the built HTML has the metas in `name`, `content` order, the client directly after `<meta charset>`, and no `</script` inside a script. **Source greps:** no `Math.random` outside `src/core/rng.js`; no `TODO`, `FIXME`, `placeholder`, `stub`; no `alert(`, `confirm(`, `prompt(`, `window.open`, `WebSocket`, `RTCPeerConnection`; no audio file extensions or `decodeAudioData`; none of the source's names (`/wii|mii\\b|balance board/i`) outside the title constant and `src/data/about.js`; no compute nodes.\n\n*flow:* **the scripted whole-game playthrough.** From a fresh save on `?test=1&render=0`: Title → profile → tutorial → all days through the real menus with a stubbed pad and the bot in every class → ending → credits → Maintenance day → Free Play has everything. Assert days, stamps, marbles rising, tilt falling to exactly 0, music detune reaching 0. Reload mid-way and assert the save resumes. Also attract: `advance(10)` on Title starts it, it visits at least four events, a key exits it and that key isn't acted on, and one wall-clock run of 10 real seconds. Also pause and resume, restart, Dev Mode opens only from Pause.\n\n*events:* for each event and tier, with the sharp bot: it completes, the result is valid, no NaN in any body, bodies return to the baseline count after `dispose()`, a forced fall ragdolls and recovers. One run with rendering on for each event for 2 s with `WEBGPU` flags: `backend === 'webgpu'`, frames rising, no console errors. One WebKit boot through a few events: WebGL2 backend, no errors.\n\n*balance:* run bots over 3 seeds per event at Tier 1 and assert: sharp reaches Exemplary (≥85) on average, average reaches Pleasant or Adequate, clumsy reaches at least Adequate (≥40), and a bot that parks the stick exactly on the goal and never corrects stays below Exemplary in Poses (measured ✔ 75-81 on Tier 1). Fruit Hat Tier 1: sharp banking at 7 has no falls and never banking has at least one. Use this test to set each `par`. This is how the plan's \"balance is key\" gets checked without a human.\n\n*input:* every verb from the pad stub, from keys, from the mouse, same game effect. Prompts switch the same frame (read `data-glyph`). Xbox glyph option. Menus fully navigable by pad alone, by keyboard alone, by mouse alone. Hover moves the focus. Clicks activate. Options ignored while Create is held. Four pads join Group Class, each controls its own lane. Tippy Raft has a winner.\n\n*audio:* music setting defaults to 10 and the bus gain is 0.10. Render each track, sting, SFX and voice with `OfflineAudioContext`: finite, non-silent (RMS above a floor), not clipped. Check detune at tilt 0 is zero.\n\n*hub:* fetch `harness.html`, `bridge.js` and `round.js` into `tools/hub/` from the same raw folder as the client. Serve the built game beside them from an in-process `http.createServer` on `listen(0, '127.0.0.1')`, so no port is hard-coded and no process needs stopping. First confirm the page is your game. Open `harness.html?game=GAME.html&players=N&auto=1` with `WEBGPU` plus `--no-sandbox --autoplay-policy=no-user-gesture-required`, wait for `body[data-complete=\"true\"]`, read `window.__hubCheck.pass` and print failing checks. Runs: `players=1`, `players=2`, `players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5`, and the same with `&scenario=host-leave`. Also on its own: open the page, press Enter, Space, Enter, Space, assert no errors, `AIHub.active` false and something drawn. The harness calls time about 5 seconds into play, so `time-up` must work from any point, and a `result` with score 0 is valid.\n\n*ui:* at 1920×1080, walk every screen and assert: no text under 30 px in computed style, nothing outside the viewport or the 5% margin except backgrounds, at most six focusable items, a visible focus. Touch-only: Pixel 7 and iPhone profiles show the message and Settings, tap opens Settings, no other controls respond, attract runs, a key or pad clears the state. About shows every Source Information field and the three feedback lists, and matches the exit-interview file.\n\n**Art pass, by eye, at the end.** `tools/shots.mjs` with `SHOTS` at 1920×1080: title, island on Day 1 and Day 5, each event mid-play, results, jar, Age Reveal, Group Class with four dolls, Dev Mode, About. Look for lost legibility at 10 feet, sunk characters, messy ink.\n\n---\n\n## 18. Build order and cut order\n\nEach milestone ends with something playable. Commit to the order: Fruit Hat before menus, because if the core isn't fun nothing else matters. Keep everything working as you go.\n\n| # | Milestone | Done when |\n|---|---|---|\n| 0 | Skeleton | Build script, single HTML, renderer with ink, sky and sea, Rapier, the loop, hooks, `test.mjs`, session client in place |\n| 1 | The soul | Balance core, Balance Disc, doll with clips and ragdoll, input with all three devices, **Fruit Hat complete with results.** Tune until it makes you want one more go |\n| 2 | The shell | Title, menu, Who's Here, island with tilt physics, Trudy with voice, dialogue, music engine, save, pause, settings, glyphs |\n| 3 | The programme | Check-In, Wobble Age, Jar, Today's Plan, days. **Tier A events:** Poses, Log Reps, Step Class, The Cairn, Room Service, Plate Spinners, Springboard |\n| 4 | The features | Attract, Dev Mode, Group Class, Tippy Raft, hub session, touch-only, About. Passing the hub harness |\n| 5 | The ending | The Grand Hold, ending, credits, Maintenance days |\n| 6 | Tier B events, in this order | Still Water, Plank & Perch, Tug of Peace, Island Loop |\n| 7 | Polish | Juice, more lines, art pass, full tests, exit interview, final build |\n\n**Cut order if you run short. Cut whole things, never stub them, and leave no trace (TASK.md: no stubs, no placeholders).** First Island Loop, then Tug of Peace, then Plank & Perch, then Still Water, then Tier 3 of each event (leaving a two-tier ladder), then Tier 2. Do not cut: Fruit Hat, Poses, Check-In, Trudy, the tilting island, the jar, the finale, Attract, Dev Mode, Group Class, the hub session, glyphs, audio. The day table builds from the registry, so cutting an event needs no other change.\n\n---\n\n## 19. Done\n\nBefore you finish, check every line:\n\n- [ ] Single HTML where TASK.md says, opens from `file://`, no external requests, no audio files\n- [ ] WebGPU backend by default, WebGL2 fallback works, ink filter on, Rapier 0.19.3, Three R180\n- [ ] Original cast, events, art and music; title is your own random pick; nothing from section 2's lists\n- [ ] All thirteen events, or the ones left after cuts, each with tiers, an intro, results and bots\n- [ ] Programme through the ending, Wobble Age graph, jar, unlocks, Free Play\n- [ ] Controller-first; keyboard and mouse native; prompts follow last device; Xbox glyph option; no dense screens\n- [ ] Attract at 10 s, any input exits; Dev Mode from Pause with tools, live sliders and reset; touch-only message and Settings\n- [ ] Group Class 1-4 on one screen; hub harness passes at 1, 2, 4 players, on the bad network, with the host leaving; game on its own passes Enter and Space\n- [ ] Music at 10% by default; all sound in code; gibberish voices with every word on screen\n- [ ] `node tools/test.mjs full` passes; a scripted whole-game playthrough is part of it\n- [ ] No TODOs, placeholders or stubs in `src/`\n- [ ] About/Credits has Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback, as TASK.md lists them, paged in large type\n- [ ] The exit-interview file exists beside the HTML in TASK.md's exact shape, and parses\n- [ ] Your chat reply has Source Information and all three feedback sections\n\n**About screen.** `tools/build.mjs` reads the exit-interview file into `src/data/about.js` so there's one source of truth. Write that file after your tests, rebuild, rerun `ui`. During development About shows what is known so far. Credit Fredoka (SIL OFL), Three.js and Rapier.\n\n**Filling in the exit interview.** Suggested: `type` Game, `genre` Sports, `source` Wii Fit, `series` empty (the franchise is the source itself, and the hub's catalogue wants it empty then), `players` 1–4, `tags` such as 3d, comedy, third-person, versus, arcade. `controls` can reuse the how-to line. Genre and perspective wording: section 1. Online: AI Hub Session Protocol v1 in ghost mode, 1-4 devices; plus 1-4 on one screen. Plan research (your own goes beside it): the hub's protocol pages and code; background on the source from Wikipedia, a Nintendo World Report review and Nintendo's Iwata Asks interviews, read as search summaries.\n\n---\n\n## 20. What was and wasn't verified\n\n**Tested here on 2026-11-04 (✔ above), with throwaway spikes:** versions exist on npm and jsDelivr; single-file esbuild build from `file://`; WebGPU in Chromium with SwiftShader; WebGL2 fallback in Chromium and WebKit; `toonOutlinePass` with MRT and the custom ink pass; instanced toon meshes and toon glass; shadow settings; the look of all characters and three palettes; the hub harness with WebGPU, own card and ghost mode; client hash; balance model; torque limit; gusts and flail; Fruit Hat as a full simulation with bots; Poses and The Cairn at all tiers with bots; tray and tumblers while walking; log on saddle; marble pours; ragdoll; tilted-gravity island; touch media queries; Fredoka's licence and file names.\n\n**Not tested. These are starting values, and they are your call:** Plate Spinners' bands, Step Class's windows, Springboard's numbers, Log Reps' ribbon, Plank's gull forces, Tug's power, Tippy Raft's gain, the noon palette, the walrus and heron animation. I could not listen to anything: the music is specified by theory, so check it with the audio tests and trust the arrangement. Nobody has played any of this with a real controller on a real TV.\n","numLines":84,"startLine":698,"totalLines":781}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01TPNSSwArf6j189RFJdxmf4","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
