{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjD1WTSeJw2UkyX8bXFq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`PLAN.md` and `planner-exit-interview.json` are written, and the plan covers everything `TASK.md` asks for. It leaves the title and `TASK.md`'s file names to the builders, with paths relative to the dev folder. I checked coverage by reading the plan against `TASK.md` and searching it for each requirement. Nothing is committed, and my scratch folder is deleted.\n\n## The game\nIt's an original game, not a recreation: a wooden-toy wellness retreat on an island balanced on one rock, crooked for as long as anyone remembers.\n\n- **Characters:** you're a jointed peg doll. Trudy, a fussy talking spirit level whose bubble is her eye, checks you in each morning and tells you your Wobble Age. The instructors are a serene heron and a walrus who can't stop believing in you.\n- **Events:** thirteen original classes plus a finale, such as Fruit Hat, where you decide when to bank your fruit before the weight topples you. They replace all of Wii Fit's activities.\n- **Progress you can see:** each class pours marbles into a jar and the island straightens. The music is slightly out of tune until the island is level.\n- **Multiplayer:** 1–4 players on one TV, plus AI Hub sessions in ghost mode.\n\nThe plan also gives a build order and a cut order, so a less capable builder can still ship something complete with no stubs.\n\n## What I tested\nI ran throwaway prototypes on this computer so the plan's main numbers and recipes are tested rather than guessed, and marked each with ✔. That turned up problems a builder would otherwise have hit:\n\n- **Stick too easy:** parking the stick on a target scored 100%, so I added a slow body sway the player has to counter.\n- **Hidden lean limit:** the doll's own collider hitting the ground limited lean to about 8° and made everything feel dead.\n- **Stacking stones:** convex-hull stones collapse on their own, while plain boxes hold.\n- **Blank screenshots:** the WebGPU flags in `TASK.md` give black screenshots; two extra flags give real ones, at about 6 fps.\n- **Hub harness:** a game with a long intro fails unless ghost traffic and progress start in the first seconds of play.\n- **Hub session:** a minimal WebGPU ghost game passed all 16 harness checks at 1, 2 and 4 players, on a bad network and with the host leaving.\n\n**Correction:** earlier I said the tilted-gravity island was \"far more stable\" than a moving platform, citing 0.004 m against 0.17 m. That comparison wasn't fair, because most of the 0.17 m was the platform really tilting. Gravity tilt is still the better choice because it's simpler, and the plan now says that instead.\n\n## What isn't tested\n- **Starting values only:** Plate Spinners, Step Class timing, Springboard, parts of Log Reps and all character animation.\n- **Music and voices:** I can't hear audio here, so they're specified by theory only.\n- **Real hardware:** nobody has played any of this on a real controller and TV.\n- **One inference:** \"multiplayer on its own\" isn't defined anywhere, so I took it to mean couch play from a line in the hub's docs. I raised this in the exit interview.\n\n## Files are in the run's `work` folder\n- `PLAN.md`\n- `planner-exit-interview.json`\n\nSources (read as search summaries, not full pages):\n- [Wii Fit, Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wii_Fit)\n- [Iwata Asks: Wii Fit, part 3, page 2](https://iwataasks.nintendo.com/interviews/wii/wii_fit/3/2)\n- [Iwata Asks: Wii Fit, part 3, page 4](https://iwataasks.nintendo.com/interviews/wii/wii_fit/3/4)\n- [Nintendo World Report review](https://nintendoworldreport.com/review/16177/wii-fit-wii)\n- [AI Hub Session Protocol](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/README.md)"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1296,"cache_read_input_tokens":461995,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1296},"output_tokens":706,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"19307802-7215-43fb-a84b-6c94bbc636c5","uuid":"86d9b8d2-e4bd-4244-b17b-f7e6de10cbb8","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:12:31.849Z","request_id":"req_011CgjD1WAbKV44LAywoFs5G"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Stop hook feedback:\n[Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says. Done when: PLAN.md covers everything TASK.md asks for.]: PLAN.md was written and covers much of TASK.md, but the transcript shows it does not cover everything TASK.md asks for. TASK.md requires a Testing section where the plan spells out allowed testing parameters and the testing rules (it does include a test section), but it also requires the plan to match the work described, and the plan's own 'What isn't tested' section leaves key game parts unverified. More concretely, TASK.md's 'Done' and 'Source Information' requirements (Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback in an in-game About/Credits and chat reply) are only addressed as instructions to the builder, and the final assistant message gives no Engine Feedback section, so the required reporting is incomplete. The stop condition is about PLAN.md covering TASK.md, and the transcript gives no clear proof that every TASK.md requirement is explicitly covered, so the condition is not clearly satisfied."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"19307802-7215-43fb-a84b-6c94bbc636c5","uuid":"3b1b097f-2daa-4975-af77-4a969dda74a1","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:12:40.878Z","isSynthetic":true}
