{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjEN4kpx722xKVezHL9G","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019PiCwwHzm7w2nStY7R3U8B","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='PLAN.md'\ns=open(p,encoding='utf-8').read()\ndef sub(old,new):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(old)==1, ('COUNT %d: '%s.count(old))+old[:80]\n    s=s.replace(old,new)\nsub(\"Stay in the small calm zone (r .18). Calm fills a meter,\",\"Stay in the small calm zone. Calm fills a meter,\")\nsub(\"Below 40 is still a pass (\\\"Attended\\\"). Events that measure a share of the maximum (Poses, Still Water) use it directly. All others set a `par` so that form = 100 × raw/par, per tier, so the sharp bot lands 88 to 95 (section 17).\",\n    \"Below 40 is still a pass (\\\"Attended\\\"). Section 6 gives an event's form where it has its own formula. Everywhere else, form = 100 × raw / `par`, with `par` set per tier so the sharp bot lands 88 to 95 (section 17).\")\nsub(\"- *Not in the hub's set.* It needs a shared world, and the session is ghost mode. *Bot:* stay toward the centre\",\n    \"- *Scoring:* form = 40 + 30 per round won. *Not in the hub's set.* It needs a shared world, and the session is ghost mode. *Bot:* stay toward the centre\")\nsub(\"**Room Service** (the long boardwalk to the guest gazebo; chase camera from behind and above)\",\"**Room Service** (a long boardwalk out to a far cabana; chase camera from behind and above)\")\nsub(\"**Stand-ins for what this computer doesn't have.**\\n| Missing |\",\"**Stand-ins for what this computer doesn't have.**\\n\\n| Missing |\")\nopen(p,'w',encoding='utf-8').write(s)\nimport json\ne=json.load(open('planner-exit-interview.json',encoding='utf-8'))\nfor x in e:\n    if x['question']=='What was the hardest thing to do?':\n        x['answer']=\"Translating a game whose identity is a physical balance board into something a thumb on a stick can't trivially beat, while keeping it original. My first test showed that simply parking the stick on the target scored 100%, because a thumb is far steadier than a body, and it took a slow-sway model to make holding still a real game. Getting the numbers right was close behind: when I simulated each event with bots, most of my first values were wrong, some badly (nobody could lose Plate Spinners, nobody could win Tug of Peace, and one Check-In test was impossible). Writing for builders whose capability and budget I don't know is why the plan has a build order and a cut order. And I can't hear anything here, so the music and voices are specified by theory and only checked as signals.\"\njson.dump(e,open('planner-exit-interview.json','w',encoding='utf-8'),ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)\nopen('planner-exit-interview.json','a').write('\\n')\nEOF\npython3 _scratch/audit.py | tail -3; python3 -c \"\nimport json\nd=json.load(open('planner-exit-interview.json',encoding='utf-8'))\nassert [x['question'] for x in d]==['What did you like most about this prompt?','What was confusing?','What was the hardest thing to do?','What would you change in this prompt?']\nprint('exit interview ok:',len(d),'answers')\"; echo '--- removing scratch:'; ls _scratch; rm -rf _scratch; ls -la; wc -w PLAN.md; sed -n '716,745p' PLAN.md | cut -c1-150","description":"Fix leftovers, re-run the audit, update exit interview, remove scratch"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13644,"cache_read_input_tokens":582388,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":13644},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"19307802-7215-43fb-a84b-6c94bbc636c5","uuid":"507eed78-6b48-483b-91b9-d3eb42360464","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:30:25.925Z","req