that simply parking the stick on the target scored 100%, because a thumb is far steadier than a body, and it took a slow-sway model to make holding still a real game. Getting the numbers right was close behind: when I simulated each event with bots, most of my first values were wrong, some badly (nobody could lose Plate Spinners, nobody could win Tug of Peace, and one Check-In test was impossible). Writing for builders whose capability and budget I don't know is why the plan has a build order and a cut order. And I can't hear anything here, so the music and voices are specified by theory and only checked as signals.\"\njson.dump(e,open('planner-exit-interview.json','w',encoding='utf-8'),ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)\nopen('planner-exit-interview.json','a').write('\\n')\nEOF\npython3 _scratch/audit.py | tail -3; python3 -c \"\nimport json\nd=json.load(open('planner-exit-interview.json',encoding='utf-8'))\nassert [x['question'] for x in d]==['What did you like most about this prompt?','What was confusing?','What was the hardest thing to do?','What would you change in this prompt?']\nprint('exit interview ok:',len(d),'answers')\"; echo '--- removing scratch:'; ls _scratch; rm -rf _scratch; ls -la; wc -w PLAN.md; sed -n '716,745p' PLAN.md | cut -c1-150","description":"Fix leftovers, re-run the audit, update exit interview, remove scratch"}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_019PiCwwHzm7w2nStY7R3U8B":{"cwd":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211905__xe6f2a4/work"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019PiCwwHzm7w2nStY7R3U8B","type":"tool_result","content":"exit-interview keys: 28\ncoverage rows: 54\n288 passed, 0 failed\nexit interview ok: 4 answers\n--- removing scratch:\naudit.py\nsim\ntotal 144\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 micha micha   4096 Nov  4 22:30 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 4 micha micha   4096 Nov  4 21:19 ..\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 111473 Nov  4 22:30 PLAN.md\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha    676 Nov  4 21:19 STAGE.md\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha  12443 Nov  4 21:19 TASK.md\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha   3231 Nov  4 22:30 planner-exit-interview.json\n19293 PLAN.md\n## 17. Testing\n\nFollow TASK.md's rules: scripts that play the game and check its state, including a scripted playthrough of the whole game; one command that prints on\n\n**Sharing this computer (TASK.md).** Other agents run here at the same time.\n- Keep every file inside your own folder, not `/tmp` (it's shared) or a parent folder. Don't read the folders beside yours.\n- Keep to one or two browsers at once and close them when done. \"Target closed\", \"page crashed\" or \"browser has been closed\" means memory ran out, not\n- Don't run `playwright install` or `playwright install-deps`: the browsers are already here. `npm i playwright@1.63.0` finds them ✔. `PLAYWRIGHT_HOST\n- Prefer `file://`: every test except `hub` opens the built file directly. WebGPU only works on a secure page, `file://` or `http://127.0.0.1`. A serv\n- Stop only processes you started, by their PID. Never `pkill`, `killall`, `fuser -k`, or kill whatever holds a port.\n- There is no display. A headed browser needs `xvfb-run`, and you shouldn't need one.\n\n**Stand-ins for what this computer doesn't have.**\n\n| Missing | Stand-in |\n|---|---|\n| Physical controller | Stub `navigator.getGamepads` (below) |\n| Touch device | Playwright phone and tablet profiles (Pixel 7, iPhone, iPad), tapping with `page.touchscreen` |\n| Someone to listen | `OfflineAudioContext` renders and `AnalyserNode` levels on the live mix |\n| Second player | The harness's 2-4 copies for sessions, four stubbed pads for Group Class |\n| Real iPhone or iPad | WebKit with an iPhone profile; it isn't iOS Safari, so never require more than it shows |\n| TV | Judge the 10-foot view from screenshots at 1920×1080 |\n\n**The command.** `node tools/test.mjs [group ...]`. Groups: `unit`, `flow`, `events`, `balance`, `input`, `audio`, `hub`, `ui`, `full`. It prints each\n\n**Browser flags ✔ (use these exact sets):**\n```js\nconst WEBGPU = ['--enable-unsafe-webgpu', '--enable-features=Vulkan', '--use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader'];  // ~60 fps; screenshots are black\nconst SHOTS  = [...WEBGPU, '--use-vulkan=swiftshader', '--use-angle=swiftshader'];                         // real screenshots at ~6 fps\n```","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"19307802-7215-43fb-a84b-6c94bbc636c5","uuid":"ac441b92-d8cc-43a7-a50d-897f47b53613","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:30:26.037Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"exit-interview keys: 28\ncoverage rows: 54\n288 passed, 0 failed\nexit interview ok: 4 answers\n--- removing scratch:\naudit.py\nsim\ntotal 144\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 micha micha   4096 Nov  4 22:30 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 4 micha micha   4096 Nov  4 21:19 ..\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 111473 Nov  4 22:30 PLAN.md\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha    676 Nov  4 21:19 STAGE.md\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha  12443 Nov  4 21:19 TASK.md\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha   3231 Nov  4 22:30 planner-exit-interview.json\n19293 PLAN.md\n## 17. Testing\n\nFollow TASK.md's rules: scripts that play the game and check its state, including a scripted playthrough of the whole game; one command that prints on\n\n**Sharing this computer (TASK.md).** Other agents run here at the same time.\n- Keep every file inside your own folder, not `/tmp` (it's shared) or a parent folder. Don't read the folders beside yours.\n- Keep to one or two browsers at once and close them when done. \"Target closed\", \"page crashed\" or \"browser has been closed\" means memory ran out, not\n- Don't run `playwright install` or `playwright install-deps`: the browsers are already here. `npm i playwright@1.63.0` finds them ✔. `PLAYWRIGHT_HOST\n- Prefer `file://`: every test except `hub` opens the built file directly. WebGPU only works on a secure page, `file://` or `http://127.0.0.1`. A serv\n- Stop only processes you started, by their PID. Never `pkill`, `killall`, `fuser -k`, or kill whatever holds a port.\n- There is no display. A headed browser needs `xvfb-run`, and you shouldn't need one.\n\n**Stand-ins for what this computer doesn't have.**\n\n| Missing | Stand-in |\n|---|---|\n| Physical controller | Stub `navigator.getGamepads` (below) |\n| Touch device | Playwright phone and tablet profiles (Pixel 7, iPhone, iPad), tapping with `page.touchscreen` |\n| Someone to listen | `OfflineAudioContext` renders and `AnalyserNode` levels on the live mix |\n| Second player | The harness's 2-4 copies for sessions, four stubbed pads for Group Class |\n| Real iPhone or iPad | WebKit with an iPhone profile; it isn't iOS Safari, so never require more than it shows |\n| TV | Judge the 10-foot view from screenshots at 1920×1080 |\n\n**The command.** `node tools/test.mjs [group ...]`. Groups: `unit`, `flow`, `events`, `balance`, `input`, `audio`, `hub`, `ui`, `full`. It prints each\n\n**Browser flags ✔ (use these exact sets):**\n```js\nconst WEBGPU = ['--enable-unsafe-webgpu', '--enable-features=Vulkan', '--use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader'];  // ~60 fps; screenshots are black\nconst SHOTS  = [...WEBGPU, '--use-vulkan=swiftshader', '--use-angle=swiftshader'];                         // real screenshots at ~6 fps\n```","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_019PiCwwHzm7w2nStY7R3U8B","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
