{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjEPeU94eNX2GwyW1kVz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`PLAN.md` now covers everything `TASK.md` asks for, and that's shown explicitly. The hook was right that my earlier keyword search proved little, and that the reporting and computer-sharing rules were only partly spelled out. `planner-exit-interview.json` is updated too, nothing is committed, and my scratch files are deleted.\n\n## What changed\n- **Coverage table:** section 21 maps all 54 `TASK.md` requirements, in order, to the section that answers them.\n- **Scripted check:** it read the 14 Source Information fields, 14 feedback questions and 28 exit-interview keys straight from `TASK.md`, and tested each against the plan. It also checked key requirement wording section by section. All 288 checks passed, but most only confirm the text is present, so I also re-read the edited sections.\n- **Reporting:** section 19 now lists every field and question builders must answer, in chat, in the About screen and in the exit-interview file.\n- **Computer rules:** section 17 now spells out the sharing rules and the stand-ins for missing hardware.\n- **Island map:** the plan now gives coordinates for every landmark.\n\n## Simulating the remaining events\nI simulated the events that still had untested numbers, using bots at three skill levels. Most of my first numbers were wrong, and these are now fixed in the plan:\n\n| Problem found | Fix |\n|---|---|\n| Plate Spinners: nobody could lose | Narrower speed bands, hoop inertia |\n| Tug of Peace: nobody could win | Much lighter rope pull |\n| Tippy Raft: rounds never ended | Swells and a faster-shrinking raft |\n| Lean Match: impossible | Scored on average error instead |\n| Room Service: tray emptied at every skill level | Smooth foot motion, gentler gusts |\n| Cairn top tier: unfair, breath didn't help | Wider stones; breath now decides it |\n| Log Reps and Plank & Perch: too easy | Tighter limits |\n| Log sliding: no usable friction setting | Made it a game rule |\n\n## What's still unverified\n- **The bots:** they are models of a person, so skill results are estimates. Only stick play was simulated, not keyboard or mouse.\n- **Partial checks:** Step Class and Plate Spinners ran as logic only. Springboard's hit chances and Island Loop are arithmetic, and the Grand Hold wasn't simulated as a whole.\n- **Not checked at all:** music and voices have never been heard, and nobody has played this on a real controller and TV.\n\n## Reporting from the planning stage\nNo game exists yet, so there's no About screen; builders report on their own builds. These answers cover my prototypes only.\n\n**Source Information**\n- **Date:** 2026-11-04 21:19:05\n- **Source:** Wii Fit\n- **Plan:** none (this stage writes it)\n- **Genre and Perspective:** physics-balance party sports with a daily-ritual progression; third person, with framed stage cameras and an orbitable chase camera\n- **Tech:** Three.js R180 (WebGPU, WebGL2 fallback, TSL toon and ink), Rapier 0.19.3, Web Audio and Gamepad API (specified, not prototyped), esbuild 0.28.2, Playwright 1.63.0, Fredoka 5.3.0\n- **Art Direction:** cel-shaded ink over a wooden-toy resort, all models made in code\n- **Animation:** specified as `AnimationMixer` clips on jointed rigs, physics-driven lean and Rapier ragdolls; only a simple test clip and the ragdoll physics were run\n- **Audio:** specified only: code-synthesised city-pop and bossa at 10% by default, Animalese and Simlish-style voices\n- **Online:** AI Hub Session Protocol v1 in ghost mode for 1–4 devices, plus 1–4 on one screen\n- **Testing:** headless prototypes and bot simulations, screenshots only for art, no subagents or workflows\n- **Research:** hub protocol pages and code; source background from search summaries\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort max\n- **Usage:** added on import\n\n**Testing Feedback**\n1. **Issues caught:** about 25.\n2. **Critical:** 7. Ground contact limiting lean, the parked stick scoring 100%, an unlosable event, an unwinnable event, endless rounds, an impossible test, and a boot snippet that wouldn't build.\n3. **Most helpful:** simulating each event with three bot skill levels.\n4. **Least helpful:** the Firefox WebGL2 checks, which changed nothing in the game.\n\n**Engine Feedback**\n1. **Liked most:** `toonOutlinePass` plus a short TSL pass gave the whole ink look, unchanged on WebGPU and WebGL2.\n2. **Stuck or guessed wrong:** yes. `hash()` given a vec2 streaked the image, toon glass turned smoky, and convex-hull stones collapsed on their own.\n3. **Most important thing built:** the balance core, a torque-limited controller on a ball joint.\n4. **Hardest part:** seeing the result. Headless WebGPU screenshots come out blank without extra flags, and those flags drop it to about 6 fps.\n5. **Changed in the engine:** none.\n6. **One change:** motors on Rapier's spherical joints in the JS API, which only single-axis joints have today.\n\n**Prompt Feedback** (full answers are in `planner-exit-interview.json`)\n1. **Liked most:** open creative choices combined with exact, checkable facts about the machine and the hub.\n2. **Confusing:** what \"the game on its own\" means for multiplayer, and \"native style\" and \"asset library\" for an engine that has neither.\n3. **Hardest:** making a balance-board game that a steady thumb can't trivially beat, while staying original.\n4. **Would change:** define standalone multiplayer, add the screenshot flags, and state how capable builders are.\n\n## Files are in the run's `work` folder\n- `PLAN.md`\n- `planner-exit-interview.json`\n\nSources (read as search summaries, not full pages):\n- [Wii Fit, Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wii_Fit)\n- [Iwata Asks: Wii Fit, part 3, page 2](https://iwataasks.nintendo.com/interviews/wii/wii_fit/3/2)\n- [Iwata Asks: Wii Fit, part 3, page 4](https://iwataasks.nintendo.com/interviews/wii/wii_fit/3/4)\n- [Nintendo World Report review](https://nintendoworldreport.com/review/16177/wii-fit-wii)\n- [AI Hub Session Protocol](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/README.md)"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3552,"cache_read_input_tokens":596032,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3552},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"19307802-7215-43fb-a84b-6c94bbc636c5","uuid":"b755c821-5188-4f42-952d-ada0b6b3022f","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:31:06.446Z","request_id":"req_011CgjEPeAmh7Ach9wkvMnhj"}
