{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjH5QzNPjj6amz2nRLLk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The hook now raises things in two categories, and I'll treat them differently.\n\n**Real and worth closing:**\n- Step Class and Plate Spinners were only simulated as logic. That hides real questions: can a soft-bodied doll even reach a lean cue within one beat at 124 BPM? Can a noisy stick actually hold a narrow speed band?\n- My audit did match phrases. A proper audit needs every clause of `TASK.md` paired with the specific instruction that answers it, judged by reading.\n\n**Can't be satisfied at this stage, and I won't fake it:** a build's own About screen and reporting. `STAGE.md` says other agents build the game \"without you\", so no build exists for those answers to describe. Inventing them would be false reporting. Nobody can hear audio here, either.\n\nI'll close the real ones, starting with those two events under real physics and stick geometry."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2992,"cache_read_input_tokens":788813,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2992},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"19307802-7215-43fb-a84b-6c94bbc636c5","uuid":"0655eb2b-9d7d-4f33-949e-d6c5494af964","timestamp":"2026-11-05T06:06:40.958Z","request_id":"req_011CgjH5Qd2vS8LdynVTGLQE"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjH5QzNPjj6amz2nRLLk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018C2JowX4TaupxFuq5PrxsT","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"mkdir -p /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211905__xe6f2a4/work/_scratch/sim && cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211905__xe6f2a4/work/_scratch/sim && npm init -y >/dev/null && npm i --no-audit --no-fund @dimforge/rapier3d-compat@0.19.3 2>&1 | tail -1 && cat > bal.mjs <<'EOF'\nimport RAPIER from '@dimforge/rapier3d-compat';\nawait RAPIER.init();\nexport { RAPIER };\nexport const V = (x = 0, y = 0, z = 0) => ({ x, y, z });\nexport const rad = (d) => (d * Math.PI) / 180, deg = (r) => (r * 180) / Math.PI;\nexport function rng(a) { a >>>= 0; return () => { a = (a + 0x6d2b79f5) >>> 0; let t = a; t = Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 15), t | 1); t ^= t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), t | 61); return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / 4294967296; }; }\nexport const DOLL = (0x0100 << 16) | 0x0010, PROP = (0x0010 << 16) | 0x0111;\nexport function makeWorld(iter = 8) { const w = new RAPIER.World(V(0, -9.81, 0)); w.timestep = 1 / 120; w.integrationParameters.numSolverIterations = iter; return w; }\nexport function makeBalancer(world, { margin = 0.45, zeta = 0.4, ankleMax = 4.6, maxLeanDeg = 18, reflex = 10, ph = 1 } = {}) {\n  const footBody = world.createRigidBody(RAPIER.RigidBodyDesc.kinematicPositionBased());\n  const body = world.createRigidBody(RAPIER.RigidBodyDesc.dynamic().setTranslation(0, 0.75, 0).setCanSleep(false).setAdditionalSolverIterations(4));\n  world.createCollider(RAPIER.ColliderDesc.capsule(0.5, 0.25).setMass(1).setCollisionGroups(DOLL), body);\n  world.createImpulseJoint(RAPIER.JointData.spherical(V(), V(0, -0.75, 0)), footBody, body, true).setContactsEnabled(false);\n  const G = 9.81 * 0.75, I = 0.75 * 0.75 + 0.06, K = G * (1 + margin), wn = Math.sqrt((K - G) / I), D = 2 * zeta * wn * I;\n  return { world, footBody, body, G, K, D, ankleMax, maxLean: rad(maxLeanDeg), reflex, ph, wishX: 0, wishZ: 0, wx: 0, wz: 0, leanX: 0, leanZ: 0, sway: 0, tremor: 0, extX: 0, extZ: 0, flailLeft: 0, flailCd: 0, flailBoost: 1.9, t: 0,\n    get cob() { return { x: this.leanX / this.maxLean, y: this.leanZ / this.maxLean }; }, get lean() { return Math.hypot(this.leanX, this.leanZ); } };\n}\nexport function stepBal(b, dt = 1 / 120) {\n  const { body, G, K, D, ph, t, sway, tremor } = b;\n  const r = 1 - Math.exp(-b.reflex * dt);\n  b.wx += (b.wishX - b.wx) * r; b.wz += (b.wishZ - b.wz) * r;\n  const tx = b.wx * b.maxLean, tz = b.wz * b.maxLean;\n  const q = body.rotation();\n  const ux = 2 * (q.x * q.y - q.w * q.z), uy = 1 - 2 * (q.x * q.x + q.z * q.z), uz = 2 * (q.y * q.z + q.w * q.x);\n  b.leanX = Math.atan2(ux, uy); b.leanZ = Math.atan2(uz, uy);\n  const w = body.angvel();\n  let Tx = -(G * Math.sin(tx) + K * (b.leanX - tx)) + D * w.z;\n  let Tz = -(G * Math.sin(tz) + K * (b.leanZ - tz)) - D * w.x;\n  const limit = b.ankleMax * (b.flailLeft > 0 ? b.flailBoost : 1);\n  const m = Math.hypot(Tx, Tz); if (m > limit) { Tx *= limit / m; Tz *= limit / m; }\n  const nx = sway * (Math.sin(t * 0.9 + ph) * 0.6 + Math.sin(t * 1.73 + ph * 2.1) * 0.4) + tremor * (Math.sin(t * 8.2 + 1.1) * 0.6 + Math.sin(t * 18.3) * 0.4) + b.extX;\n  const nz = sway * (Math.sin(t * 0.77 + ph * 1.7) * 0.6 + Math.sin(t * 1.51 + ph * 0.6) * 0.4) + tremor * (Math.sin(t * 7.1 + 2.3) * 0.6 + Math.sin(t * 15.7 + 0.7) * 0.4) + b.extZ;\n  body.resetTorques(true);\n  body.addTorque(V(Tz + nz, -w.y * 0.6, -(Tx + nx)), true);\n  b.flailLeft = Math.max(0, b.flailLeft - dt); b.flailCd = Math.max(0, b.flailCd - dt); b.t += dt;\n}\nexport const avg = (a) => a.reduce((s, x) => s + x, 0) / a.length;\nEOF\ncat > step.mjs <<'EOF'\n// Step Class as a whole: the chart, feet with timing error, and lean cues judged on the real dot of the real balance core.\nimport { rng, avg, rad, deg, makeWorld, makeBalancer, stepBal } from './bal.mjs';\nconst PATTERNS = ['L...R...', 'L.R.L.R.', 'L.R.B...', 'L.L.R.R.', '<...>...', 'L.R.<...', '^...v...', 'LRL.RLR.', 'B.B.LRB.', 'L.R.LRLR'];\nfunction chart(pats, bpm, form = [[4, null], [8, 'A'], [8, 'B'], [8, 'A'], [4, 'break'], [8, 'B'], [4, null]]) {\n  const notes = []; let bar = 0; const lean = pats.filter((p) => /[<>^v]/.test(p) && !/[LRB]/.test(p)), feet = pats.filter((p) => /[LRB]/.test(p));\n  for (const [n, sec] of form) for (let i = 0; i < n; i++, bar++) { if (!sec) continue; const p = sec === 'break' ? lean[i % lean.length] : sec === 'A' ? feet[i % Math.max(1, Math.ceil(feet.length / 2))] : feet[(i + Math.floor(feet.length / 2)) % feet.length]; [...p].forEach((c, k) => { if (c !== '.') notes.push({ c, t: (bar * 4 + k / 2) * 60 / bpm }); }); }\n  return { notes, secs: bar * 4 * 60 / bpm, beat: 60 / bpm };\n}\nconst gaussF = (r) => () => Math.sqrt(-2 * Math.log(1 - r())) * Math.cos(2 * Math.PI * r());\nconst DIR = { '<': [-1, 0], '>': [1, 0], '^': [0, -1], 'v': [0, 1] };\nconst SK = { sharp: { jit: 28, lead: 0.3, react: 0, stick: 0.95, wrong: 0.005 }, average: { jit: 55, lead: 0.18, react: 0.05, stick: 0.85, wrong: 0.03 }, clumsy: { jit: 95, lead: 0.05, react: 0.15, stick: 0.75, wrong: 0.08 } };\nfunction run({ pats, bpm, skill, seed, threshold = 0.35, reflex = 10, maxLeanDeg = 18, rock = 0.1, form }) {\n  const world = makeWorld(8), b = makeBalancer(world, { ph: seed, reflex, maxLeanDeg }), r = rng(seed * 41), g = gaussF(r), S = SK[skill], { notes, secs, beat } = chart(pats, bpm, form), dt = 1 / 120;\n  b.sway = 0.03;\n  let score = 0, max = 0, leanOK = 0, leanN = 0, footScore = 0, footN = 0, late = [], peak = 0, combo = 0, best = 0, misses = 0, side = 1, rockLeft = 0;\n  const leanNotes = notes.filter((n) => DIR[n.c]).map((n) => ({ ...n, done: false, reach: null })), footNotes = notes.filter((n) => !DIR[n.c]);\n  // feet: judged by timing alone; they rock the doll a little when they land\n  for (const n of footNotes) { n.press = n.t + (g() * S.jit) / 1000; n.miss = r() < S.wrong; }\n  let fi = 0, want = { x: 0, y: 0 }, li = 0;\n  const secsAll = secs + 1;\n  for (let s = 0; s < secsAll * 120; s++) {\n    const t = s / 120;\n    while (fi < footNotes.length && t >= footNotes[fi].press) { side = -side; rockLeft = 0.1; fi++; }\n    b.extX = rockLeft > 0 ? rock * side : 0; rockLeft -= dt;\n    // lean: the player sees the ribbon coming and starts early by their lead, plus timing error\n    const cue = leanNotes.find((n) => !n.started && t >= n.t - S.lead + (n.err ??= (g() * S.jit) / 1000));\n    if (cue) { cue.started = true; const d = DIR[cue.c]; want = { x: d[0] * S.stick, y: d[1] * S.stick }; cue.releaseAt = cue.t + 2 * beat - 0.05; }\n    const active = [...leanNotes].reverse().find((n) => n.started); if (active && t >= active.releaseAt && !leanNotes.some((n) => n.started && n !== active && t < n.releaseAt)) want = { x: 0, y: 0 };\n    b.wishX = want.x; b.wishZ = want.y; stepBal(b, dt); world.step(); peak = Math.max(peak, b.lean);\n    const c = b.cob;\n    for (const n of leanNotes) { if (n.reach !== null || t < n.t - 0.2) continue; const d = DIR[n.c]; if (c.x * d[0] + c.y * d[1] >= threshold) n.reach = t - n.t; if (t > n.t + 2 * beat) n.reach = Infinity; }\n  }\n  for (const n of footNotes) { const e = Math.abs(n.press - n.t) * 1000, v = n.miss || e > 135 ? 0 : e <= 45 ? 1 : e <= 90 ? 0.7 : 0.4; footScore += v; footN++; if (v === 0) { misses++; combo = 0; } else { combo++; best = Math.max(best, combo); } }\n  for (const n of leanNotes) { leanN++; const v = n.reach === null || n.reach === Infinity ? 0 : n.reach <= beat ? 1 : n.reach <= 1.5 * beat ? 0.7 : 0.4; leanOK += v; if (n.reach !== Infinity && n.reach !== null) late.push(n.reach); }\n  world.free();\n  const total = (footScore + leanOK) / (footN + leanN);\n  return { form: 100 * total, feet: 100 * footScore / Math.max(1, footN), lean: leanN ? 100 * leanOK / leanN : null, reach: late.length ? avg(late) : null, beat, peak: deg(peak), leanN, footN, secs };\n}\nconst T1 = PATTERNS.slice(0, 3).concat('<...>...'), T2 = PATTERNS.slice(0, 7), T3 = PATTERNS;\nconsole.log('STEP CLASS whole: form, feet score, lean score, when the dot reaches the threshold after the cue (s) vs one beat');\nfor (const [n, pats, bpm] of [['T1 104', T1, 104], ['T2 116', T2, 116], ['T3 124', T3, 124]]) for (const th of [0.5, 0.35, 0.25]) {\n  console.log(' ', n, `threshold ${th}`.padEnd(15), ['sharp', 'average', 'clumsy'].map((sk) => { const res = [1, 2, 3].map((seed) => run({ pats, bpm, skill: sk, seed, threshold: th })); return `${sk} form ${avg(res.map((x) => x.form)).toFixed(0)} feet ${avg(res.map((x) => x.feet)).toFixed(0)} lean ${avg(res.map((x) => x.lean ?? 0)).toFixed(0)} reach ${avg(res.map((x) => x.reach ?? 0)).toFixed(2)}`; }).join(' | '), `beat ${(60 / bpm).toFixed(2)} leans ${run({ pats, bpm, skill: 'sharp', seed: 1, threshold: th }).leanN} peak ${run({ pats, bpm, skill: 'sharp', seed: 1, threshold: th }).peak.toFixed(0)}deg`);\n}\nconst sess = run({ pats: T2, bpm: 116, skill: 'average', seed: 1, form: [[2, null], [8, 'A'], [8, 'B'], [6, 'A']] });\nconsole.log('  session chart:', sess.secs.toFixed(1), 's', sess.footN, 'foot notes', sess.leanN, 'lean notes, form', sess.form.toFixed(0));\nEOF\ncat > plates3.mjs <<'EOF'\n// Plate Spinners from the real input: a stick (or mouse) vector moving in a circle, measured the way the plan says.\nimport { rng, avg } from './bal.mjs';\nfunction play({ layout, decay, gain = 0.45, skill, seed, tauM = 0.12, tauH = 0.5, secs = 60, device = 'stick' }) {\n  const bands = { L: [3.5, 5], M: [6.5, 8], S: [9.5, 11] }, r = rng(seed * 73), dt = 1 / 120;\n  const SK = { sharp: { lag: 0.12, rate: 0.03, jitter: 0.012, radius: 0.9 }, average: { lag: 0.28, rate: 0.07, jitter: 0.03, radius: 0.85 }, clumsy: { lag: 0.5, rate: 0.13, jitter: 0.06, radius: 0.78 } }[skill];\n  const ps = layout.map((k) => ({ k, e: 0.7, down: 0 }));\n  let band = null, want = 0, lagT = 0, wander = 0, phase = 0, jx = 0, jy = 0, px = null, py = null, omegaS = 0, hoop = 0, alive = 0, max = 0, crashes = 0, inBand = 0, fumbles = 0, fumbleLeft = 0, nextFumble = 6 + r() * 10, sign = 1;\n  for (let s = 0; s < secs * 120; s++) {\n    const t = s / 120; lagT -= dt;\n    if (lagT <= 0) { lagT = SK.lag; const up = ps.filter((p) => p.down <= 0); if (up.length) { const low = up.reduce((a, b) => (b.e < a.e ? b : a)); const cur = band ? up.filter((p) => p.k === band) : []; const curLow = cur.length ? Math.min(...cur.map((p) => p.e)) : 1; if (!band || curLow > 0.85 || (low.e < 0.3 && curLow > low.e + 0.15)) band = low.k; const [a, b] = bands[band]; want = (a + b) / 2; } wander += (r() - 0.5) * SK.rate; wander = Math.max(-SK.rate * 1.6, Math.min(SK.rate * 1.6, wander)); }\n    // a thumb sometimes slips off the rim of the circle for a moment\n    if (t >= nextFumble) { nextFumble = t + 6 + r() * 10; fumbleLeft = skill === 'sharp' ? 0.08 : skill === 'average' ? 0.15 : 0.3; fumbles++; }\n    phase += sign * want * (1 + wander) * dt;\n    jx += (r() - 0.5) * 0.25 * SK.jitter * 8; jy += (r() - 0.5) * 0.25 * SK.jitter * 8; jx *= 0.9; jy *= 0.9;\n    const rad = (fumbleLeft > 0 ? 0.3 : SK.radius) + 0.04 * Math.sin(t * 2.3); fumbleLeft -= dt;\n    let x = Math.cos(phase) * rad + jx, y = Math.sin(phase) * rad + jy; const L = Math.hypot(x, y); if (L > 1) { x /= L; y /= L; }\n    // the plan's measure: angular velocity of the weight vector while |weight| > .5, smoothed; otherwise it decays. Then hoop inertia.\n    if (Math.hypot(x, y) > 0.5 && px !== null && Math.hypot(px, py) > 0.5) { let d = Math.atan2(y, x) - Math.atan2(py, px); if (d > Math.PI) d -= 2 * Math.PI; if (d < -Math.PI) d += 2 * Math.PI; omegaS += (d / dt - omegaS) * (1 - Math.exp(-dt / tauM)); } else omegaS *= Math.exp(-3 * dt);\n    px = x; py = y;\n    hoop += (Math.abs(omegaS) - hoop) * (1 - Math.exp(-dt / tauH));\n    let any = false;\n    for (const p of ps) { if (p.down > 0) { p.down -= dt; if (p.down <= 0) p.e = 0.7; continue; } const [a, b] = bands[p.k]; if (hoop >= a && hoop < b) { p.e = Math.min(1, p.e + gain * dt); any = true; } p.e -= decay * dt; if (p.e <= 0) { p.down = 6; crashes++; } alive += dt; }\n    if (any) inBand += dt; max += ps.length * dt;\n  }\n  return { share: alive / max, crashes, inBand: inBand / secs };\n}\nconsole.log('PLATE SPINNERS from a moving stick vector: share alive, crashes, time with the hoop in some band');\nfor (const [n, c] of [['T1', { layout: ['L', 'M', 'S'], decay: 0.11 }], ['T2', { layout: ['L', 'M', 'M', 'S'], decay: 0.13 }], ['T3', { layout: ['L', 'L', 'M', 'M', 'S', 'S'], decay: 0.16 }]]) for (const tauM of [0.05, 0.12, 0.25]) {\n  console.log(' ', n, `measure smoothing ${tauM}`.padEnd(24), ['sharp', 'average', 'clumsy'].map((sk) => { const res = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6].map((seed) => play({ ...c, skill: sk, seed, tauM })); return `${sk} ${(100 * avg(res.map((x) => x.share))).toFixed(0)}% cr${avg(res.map((x) => x.crashes)).toFixed(1)} band ${(100 * avg(res.map((x) => x.inBand))).toFixed(0)}%`; }).join(' | '));\n}\nEOF\nnode step.mjs 2>&1 | grep -v deprecated | cut -c1-230; node plates3.mjs 2>&1 | grep -v deprecated | cut -c1-200","description":"Simulate Step Class on the real balance core and Plate Spinners from a stick vector","timeout":500000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2992,"cache_read_input_tokens":788813,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2992},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"19307802-7215-43fb-a84b-6c94bbc636c5","uuid":"45ba9fdf-14ac-468a-bcf4-266afd3d3478","timestamp":"2026-11-05T06:07:31.395Z","request_id":"req_011CgjH5Qd2vS8LdynVTGLQE","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_018C2JowX4TaupxFuq5PrxsT":{"command":"mkdir -p /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211905__xe6f2a4/work/_scratch/sim && cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211905__xe6f2a4/work/_scratch/sim && npm init -y >/dev/null && npm i --no-audit --no-fund @dimforge/rapier3d-compat@0.19.3 2>&1 | tail -1 && cat > bal.mjs <<'EOF'\nimport RAPIER from '@dimforge/rapier3d-compat';\nawait RAPIER.init();\nexport { RAPIER };\nexport const V = (x = 0, y = 0, z = 0) => ({ x, y, z });\nexport const rad = (d) => (d * Math.PI) / 180, deg = (r) => (r * 180) / Math.PI;\nexport function rng(a) { a >>>= 0; return () => { a = (a + 0x6d2b79f5) >>> 0; let t = a; t = Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 15), t | 1); t ^= t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), t | 61); return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / 4294967296; }; }\nexport const DOLL = (0x0100 << 16) | 0x0010, PROP = (0x0010 << 16) | 0x0111;\nexport function makeWorld(iter = 8) { const w = new RAPIER.World(V(0, -9.81, 0)); w.timestep = 1 / 120; w.integrationParameters.numSolverIterations = iter; return w; }\nexport function makeBalancer(world, { margin = 0.45, zeta = 0.4, ankleMax = 4.6, maxLeanDeg = 18, reflex = 10, ph = 1 } = {}) {\n  const footBody = world.createRigidBody(RAPIER.RigidBodyDesc.kinematicPositionBased());\n  const body = world.createRigidBody(RAPIER.RigidBodyDesc.dynamic().setTranslation(0, 0.75, 0).setCanSleep(false).setAdditionalSolverIterations(4));\n  world.createCollider(RAPIER.ColliderDesc.capsule(0.5, 0.25).setMass(1).setCollisionGroups(DOLL), body);\n  world.createImpulseJoint(RAPIER.JointData.spherical(V(), V(0, -0.75, 0)), footBody, body, true).setContactsEnabled(false);\n  const G = 9.81 * 0.75, I = 0.75 * 0.75 + 0.06, K = G * (1 + margin), wn = Math.sqrt((K - G) / I), D = 2 * zeta * wn * I;\n  return { world, footBody, body, G, K, D, ankleMax, maxLean: rad(maxLeanDeg), reflex, ph, wishX: 0, wishZ: 0, wx: 0, wz: 0, leanX: 0, leanZ: 0, sway: 0, tremor: 0, extX: 0, extZ: 0, flailLeft: 0, flailCd: 0, flailBoost: 1.9, t: 0,\n    get cob() { return { x: this.leanX / this.maxLean, y: this.leanZ / this.maxLean }; }, get lean() { return Math.hypot(this.leanX, this.leanZ); } };\n}\nexport function stepBal(b, dt = 1 / 120) {\n  const { body, G, K, D, ph, t, sway, tremor } = b;\n  const r = 1 - Math.exp(-b.reflex * dt);\n  b.wx += (b.wishX - b.wx) * r; b.wz += (b.wishZ - b.wz) * r;\n  const tx = b.wx * b.maxLean, tz = b.wz * b.maxLean;\n  const q = body.rotation();\n  const ux = 2 * (q.x * q.y - q.w * q.z), uy = 1 - 2 * (q.x * q.x + q.z * q.z), uz = 2 * (q.y * q.z + q.w * q.x);\n  b.leanX = Math.atan2(ux, uy); b.leanZ = Math.atan2(uz, uy);\n  const w = body.angvel();\n  let Tx = -(G * Math.sin(tx) + K * (b.leanX - tx)) + D * w.z;\n  let Tz = -(G * Math.sin(tz) + K * (b.leanZ - tz)) - D * w.x;\n  const limit = b.ankleMax * (b.flailLeft > 0 ? b.flailBoost : 1);\n  const m = Math.hypot(Tx, Tz); if (m > limit) { Tx *= limit / m; Tz *= limit / m; }\n  const nx = sway * (Math.sin(t * 0.9 + ph) * 0.6 + Math.sin(t * 1.73 + ph * 2.1) * 0.4) + tremor * (Math.sin(t * 8.2 + 1.1) * 0.6 + Math.sin(t * 18.3) * 0.4) + b.extX;\n  const nz = sway * (Math.sin(t * 0.77 + ph * 1.7) * 0.6 + Math.sin(t * 1.51 + ph * 0.6) * 0.4) + tremor * (Math.sin(t * 7.1 + 2.3) * 0.6 + Math.sin(t * 15.7 + 0.7) * 0.4) + b.extZ;\n  body.resetTorques(true);\n  body.addTorque(V(Tz + nz, -w.y * 0.6, -(Tx + nx)), true);\n  b.flailLeft = Math.max(0, b.flailLeft - dt); b.flailCd = Math.max(0, b.flailCd - dt); b.t += dt;\n}\nexport const avg = (a) => a.reduce((s, x) => s + x, 0) / a.length;\nEOF\ncat > step.mjs <<'EOF'\n// Step Class as a whole: the chart, feet with timing error, and lean cues judged on the real dot of the real balance core.\nimport { rng, avg, rad, deg, makeWorld, makeBalancer, stepBal } from './bal.mjs';\nconst PATTERNS = ['L...R...', 'L.R.L.R.', 'L.R.B...', 'L.L.R.R.', '<...>...', 'L.R.<...', '^...v...', 'LRL.RLR.', 'B.B.LRB.', 'L.R.LRLR'];\nfunction chart(pats, bpm, form = [[4, null], [8, 'A'], [8, 'B'], [8, 'A'], [4, 'break'], [8, 'B'], [4, null]]) {\n  const notes = []; let bar = 0; const lean = pats.filter((p) => /[<>^v]/.test(p) && !/[LRB]/.test(p)), feet = pats.filter((p) => /[LRB]/.test(p));\n  for (const [n, sec] of form) for (let i = 0; i < n; i++, bar++) { if (!sec) continue; const p = sec === 'break' ? lean[i % lean.length] : sec === 'A' ? feet[i % Math.max(1, Math.ceil(feet.length / 2))] : feet[(i + Math.floor(feet.length / 2)) % feet.length]; [...p].forEach((c, k) => { if (c !== '.') notes.push({ c, t: (bar * 4 + k / 2) * 60 / bpm }); }); }\n  return { notes, secs: bar * 4 * 60 / bpm, beat: 60 / bpm };\n}\nconst gaussF = (r) => () => Math.sqrt(-2 * Math.log(1 - r())) * Math.cos(2 * Math.PI * r());\nconst DIR = { '<': [-1, 0], '>': [1, 0], '^': [0, -1], 'v': [0, 1] };\nconst SK = { sharp: { jit: 28, lead: 0.3, react: 0, stick: 0.95, wrong: 0.005 }, average: { jit: 55, lead: 0.18, react: 0.05, stick: 0.85, wrong: 0.03 }, clumsy: { jit: 95, lead: 0.05, react: 0.15, stick: 0.75, wrong: 0.08 } };\nfunction run({ pats, bpm, skill, seed, threshold = 0.35, reflex = 10, maxLeanDeg = 18, rock = 0.1, form }) {\n  const world = makeWorld(8), b = makeBalancer(world, { ph: seed, reflex, maxLeanDeg }), r = rng(seed * 41), g = gaussF(r), S = SK[skill], { notes, secs, beat } = chart(pats, bpm, form), dt = 1 / 120;\n  b.sway = 0.03;\n  let score = 0, max = 0, leanOK = 0, leanN = 0, footScore = 0, footN = 0, late = [], peak = 0, combo = 0, best = 0, misses = 0, side = 1, rockLeft = 0;\n  const leanNotes = notes.filter((n) => DIR[n.c]).map((n) => ({ ...n, done: false, reach: null })), footNotes = notes.filter((n) => !DIR[n.c]);\n  // feet: judged by timing alone; they rock the doll a little when they land\n  for (const n of footNotes) { n.press = n.t + (g() * S.jit) / 1000; n.miss = r() < S.wrong; }\n  let fi = 0, want = { x: 0, y: 0 }, li = 0;\n  const secsAll = secs + 1;\n  for (let s = 0; s < secsAll * 120; s++) {\n    const t = s / 120;\n    while (fi < footNotes.length && t >= footNotes[fi].press) { side = -side; rockLeft = 0.1; fi++; }\n    b.extX = rockLeft > 0 ? rock * side : 0; rockLeft -= dt;\n    // lean: the player sees the ribbon coming and starts early by their lead, plus timing error\n    const cue = leanNotes.find((n) => !n.started && t >= n.t - S.lead + (n.err ??= (g() * S.jit) / 1000));\n    if (cue) { cue.started = true; const d = DIR[cue.c]; want = { x: d[0] * S.stick, y: d[1] * S.stick }; cue.releaseAt = cue.t + 2 * beat - 0.05; }\n    const active = [...leanNotes].reverse().find((n) => n.started); if (active && t >= active.releaseAt && !leanNotes.some((n) => n.started && n !== active && t < n.releaseAt)) want = { x: 0, y: 0 };\n    b.wishX = want.x; b.wishZ = want.y; stepBal(b, dt); world.step(); peak = Math.max(peak, b.lean);\n    const c = b.cob;\n    for (const n of leanNotes) { if (n.reach !== null || t < n.t - 0.2) continue; const d = DIR[n.c]; if (c.x * d[0] + c.y * d[1] >= threshold) n.reach = t - n.t; if (t > n.t + 2 * beat) n.reach = Infinity; }\n  }\n  for (const n of footNotes) { const e = Math.abs(n.press - n.t) * 1000, v = n.miss || e > 135 ? 0 : e <= 45 ? 1 : e <= 90 ? 0.7 : 0.4; footScore += v; footN++; if (v === 0) { misses++; combo = 0; } else { combo++; best = Math.max(best, combo); } }\n  for (const n of leanNotes) { leanN++; const v = n.reach === null || n.reach === Infinity ? 0 : n.reach <= beat ? 1 : n.reach <= 1.5 * beat ? 0.7 : 0.4; leanOK += v; if (n.reach !== Infinity && n.reach !== null) late.push(n.reach); }\n  world.free();\n  const total = (footScore + leanOK) / (footN + leanN);\n  return { form: 100 * total, feet: 100 * footScore / Math.max(1, footN), lean: leanN ? 100 * leanOK / leanN : null, reach: late.length ? avg(late) : null, beat, peak: deg(peak), leanN, footN, secs };\n}\nconst T1 = PATTERNS.slice(0, 3).concat('<...>...'), T2 = PATTERNS.slice(0, 7), T3 = PATTERNS;\nconsole.log('STEP CLASS whole: form, feet score, lean score, when the dot reaches the threshold after the cue (s) vs one beat');\nfor (const [n, pats, bpm] of [['T1 104', T1, 104], ['T2 116', T2, 116], ['T3 124', T3, 124]]) for (const th of [0.5, 0.35, 0.25]) {\n  console.log(' ', n, `threshold ${th}`.padEnd(15), ['sharp', 'average', 'clumsy'].map((sk) => { const res = [1, 2, 3].map((seed) => run({ pats, bpm, skill: sk, seed, threshold: th })); return `${sk} form ${avg(res.map((x) => x.form)).toFixed(0)} feet ${avg(res.map((x) => x.feet)).toFixed(0)} lean ${avg(res.map((x) => x.lean ?? 0)).toFixed(0)} reach ${avg(res.map((x) => x.reach ?? 0)).toFixed(2)}`; }).join(' | '), `beat ${(60 / bpm).toFixed(2)} leans ${run({ pats, bpm, skill: 'sharp', seed: 1, threshold: th }).leanN} peak ${run({ pats, bpm, skill: 'sharp', seed: 1, threshold: th }).peak.toFixed(0)}deg`);\n}\nconst sess = run({ pats: T2, bpm: 116, skill: 'average', seed: 1, form: [[2, null], [8, 'A'], [8, 'B'], [6, 'A']] });\nconsole.log('  session chart:', sess.secs.toFixed(1), 's', sess.footN, 'foot notes', sess.leanN, 'lean notes, form', sess.form.toFixed(0));\nEOF\ncat > plates3.mjs <<'EOF'\n// Plate Spinners from the real input: a stick (or mouse) vector moving in a circle, measured the way the plan says.\nimport { rng, avg } from './bal.mjs';\nfunction play({ layout, decay, gain = 0.45, skill, seed, tauM = 0.12, tauH = 0.5, secs = 60, device = 'stick' }) {\n  const bands = { L: [3.5, 5], M: [6.5, 8], S: [9.5, 11] }, r = rng(seed * 73), dt = 1 / 120;\n  const SK = { sharp: { lag: 0.12, rate: 0.03, jitter: 0.012, radius: 0.9 }, average: { lag: 0.28, rate: 0.07, jitter: 0.03, radius: 0.85 }, clumsy: { lag: 0.5, rate: 0.13, jitter: 0.06, radius: 0.78 } }[skill];\n  const ps = layout.map((k) => ({ k, e: 0.7, down: 0 }));\n  let band = null, want = 0, lagT = 0, wander = 0, phase = 0, jx = 0, jy = 0, px = null, py = null, omegaS = 0, hoop = 0, alive = 0, max = 0, crashes = 0, inBand = 0, fumbles = 0, fumbleLeft = 0, nextFumble = 6 + r() * 10, sign = 1;\n  for (let s = 0; s < secs * 120; s++) {\n    const t = s / 120; lagT -= dt;\n    if (lagT <= 0) { lagT = SK.lag; const up = ps.filter((p) => p.down <= 0); if (up.length) { const low = up.reduce((a, b) => (b.e < a.e ? b : a)); const cur = band ? up.filter((p) => p.k === band) : []; const curLow = cur.length ? Math.min(...cur.map((p) => p.e)) : 1; if (!band || curLow > 0.85 || (low.e < 0.3 && curLow > low.e + 0.15)) band = low.k; const [a, b] = bands[band]; want = (a + b) / 2; } wander += (r() - 0.5) * SK.rate; wander = Math.max(-SK.rate * 1.6, Math.min(SK.rate * 1.6, wander)); }\n    // a thumb sometimes slips off the rim of the circle for a moment\n    if (t >= nextFumble) { nextFumble = t + 6 + r() * 10; fumbleLeft = skill === 'sharp' ? 0.08 : skill === 'average' ? 0.15 : 0.3; fumbles++; }\n    phase += sign * want * (1 + wander) * dt;\n    jx += (r() - 0.5) * 0.25 * SK.jitter * 8; jy += (r() - 0.5) * 0.25 * SK.jitter * 8; jx *= 0.9; jy *= 0.9;\n    const rad = (fumbleLeft > 0 ? 0.3 : SK.radius) + 0.04 * Math.sin(t * 2.3); fumbleLeft -= dt;\n    let x = Math.cos(phase) * rad + jx, y = Math.sin(phase) * rad + jy; const L = Math.hypot(x, y); if (L > 1) { x /= L; y /= L; }\n    // the plan's measure: angular velocity of the weight vector while |weight| > .5, smoothed; otherwise it decays. Then hoop inertia.\n    if (Math.hypot(x, y) > 0.5 && px !== null && Math.hypot(px, py) > 0.5) { let d = Math.atan2(y, x) - Math.atan2(py, px); if (d > Math.PI) d -= 2 * Math.PI; if (d < -Math.PI) d += 2 * Math.PI; omegaS += (d / dt - omegaS) * (1 - Math.exp(-dt / tauM)); } else omegaS *= Math.exp(-3 * dt);\n    px = x; py = y;\n    hoop += (Math.abs(omegaS) - hoop) * (1 - Math.exp(-dt / tauH));\n    let any = false;\n    for (const p of ps) { if (p.down > 0) { p.down -= dt; if (p.down <= 0) p.e = 0.7; continue; } const [a, b] = bands[p.k]; if (hoop >= a && hoop < b) { p.e = Math.min(1, p.e + gain * dt); any = true; } p.e -= decay * dt; if (p.e <= 0) { p.down = 6; crashes++; } alive += dt; }\n    if (any) inBand += dt; max += ps.length * dt;\n  }\n  return { share: alive / max, crashes, inBand: inBand / secs };\n}\nconsole.log('PLATE SPINNERS from a moving stick vector: share alive, crashes, time with the hoop in some band');\nfor (const [n, c] of [['T1', { layout: ['L', 'M', 'S'], decay: 0.11 }], ['T2', { layout: ['L', 'M', 'M', 'S'], decay: 0.13 }], ['T3', { layout: ['L', 'L', 'M', 'M', 'S', 'S'], decay: 0.16 }]]) for (const tauM of [0.05, 0.12, 0.25]) {\n  console.log(' ', n, `measure smoothing ${tauM}`.padEnd(24), ['sharp', 'average', 'clumsy'].map((sk) => { const res = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6].map((seed) => play({ ...c, skill: sk, seed, tauM })); return `${sk} ${(100 * avg(res.map((x) => x.share))).toFixed(0)}% cr${avg(res.map((x) => x.crashes)).toFixed(1)} band ${(100 * avg(res.map((x) => x.inBand))).toFixed(0)}%`; }).join(' | '));\n}\nEOF\nnode step.mjs 2>&1 | grep -v deprecated | cut -c1-230; node plates3.mjs 2>&1 | grep -v deprecated | cut -c1-200","description":"Simulate Step Class on the real balance core and Plate Spinners from a stick vector","timeout":500000}}}
