{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjHGHjbpfhr3K1rXyLZZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Y5DWZXtE5CMtKHEuxgNCM7","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='PLAN.md'\ns=open(p,encoding='utf-8').read()\ndef sub(old,new):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(old)==1, ('COUNT %d: '%s.count(old))+old[:90]\n    s=s.replace(old,new)\n# Step Class\nsub(\"- *Windows (starting values):* Perfect ±45 ms, Good ±90, OK ±135.\",\"- *Windows ✔:* Perfect ±45 ms, Good ±90, OK ±135 for feet.\")\nsub(\"Session version: 24 bars at 116.\",\"Session version: 24 bars at 116, with a 4-bar lean break.\")\na=s.index(\"- *Scoring ✔:* Perfect 1, Good .7, OK .4; form is the share of the maximum.\")\nb=s.index(\"- *Bot:* hits every note with its skill's timing error.\")\ns=s[:a]+\"\"\"- *Lean notes are judged differently ✔.* A soft-bodied doll physically can't get its dot across in one beat: in Tier 1's break, which swings end to end, it takes .6-.9 s against a .58 s beat, so even a perfect player would be marked late. A lean note scores when the dot passes .25 in that direction: full marks within 1.5 beats, half within 2. The ribbon scrolls toward you, so players can lead it with the stick.\n- *Scoring ✔ (whole run on the real balance core):* feet Perfect 1, Good .7, OK .4; form is the share of the maximum. With timing error sd 28 / 55 / 95 ms and a small miss rate: Tier 1 97 / 84 / 62, Tier 2 97 / 85 / 64, Tier 3 97 / 84 / 63, with lean notes at 100 / 97 / 67, 100 / 100 / 88 and 100 / 96 / 84. The tiers have 106 notes in 102 s, 108 in 91 s and 126 in 85 s, with no falls (peak lean 24-26°). The session version takes 49.7 s, with 54 foot and 10 lean notes, and fits its 50 s slot: 98 / 88 / 69.\n\"\"\"+s[b:]\n# Plate Spinners\nsub(\"- *Measure:* hoop ω = smoothed angular velocity of the weight vector when |weight| > 0.5; otherwise it decays.\",\"- *Measure:* hoop ω = angular velocity of the weight vector when |weight| > 0.5, smoothed with τ = .12 s; otherwise it decays at 3 /s.\")\nsub(\"- *Tiers ✔, 60 s:* start energy .7, gain .45 per s. Tier 1: L M S, decay .11. Tier 2: L M M S, decay .13. Tier 3: L L M M S S, decay .16. Share of plate-time alive: Tier 1 100% / 87% / 73%, Tier 2 90 / 80 / 67, Tier 3 79 / 70 / 61. Crashes a minute: 0 / 4 / 8 on Tier 1, more above.\",\n    \"- *Tiers ✔, 60 s:* start energy .7, gain .45 per s. Tier 1: L M S, decay .11. Tier 2: L M M S, decay .13. Tier 3: L L M M S S, decay .16. Share of plate-time alive, from a simulated stick moving in a circle with hand jitter, rate wander and slips, measured as above: Tier 1 100% / 89% / 82%, Tier 2 89 / 86 / 74, Tier 3 79 / 76 / 66. Crashes a minute: 0 / 3.5 / 6 on Tier 1, more above. The smoothing isn't critical (.05 to .25 s gives much the same).\")\nsub(\"- *Scoring:* form = `200 × share − 100`, floored at 0 ✔ Tier 1 100 / 74 / 46.\",\"- *Scoring:* form = `200 × share − 100`, floored at 0 ✔ Tier 1 100 / 78 / 64.\")\n# clause 30, 31\nsub(\"**Stack.** `three@0.180.0`\",\"**Where things go.** Keep all your dev files in the subfolder TASK.md names (your dev folder). Develop separate modules there, and bundle them into the single HTML file in the root, named as TASK.md says, when you're done. TASK.md allows external CDN dependencies; this plan inlines everything instead, so the file works offline and inside the hub.\\n\\n**Stack.** `three@0.180.0`\")\n# clause 75\nsub(\"| Second player | The harness's 2-4 copies for sessions, four stubbed pads for Group Class |\",\"| Second player | TASK.md suggests two browser pages. The hub's harness is that test, built for this: it plays 2-4 copies at once, in frames of one page, on a simulated network. Add four stubbed pads for Group Class |\")\n# clause 91\nsub(\"**Flow.** Intro Card (name, one sentence, one diagram, this device's prompts; Use to begin)\",\"**What you can and can't do.** Every Intro Card and the How to Play page say what you can do here and, in one line, what you can't: \\\"You can't fall in this one.\\\" \\\"Your feet don't matter here.\\\" \\\"You can't lose this; you can only do it badly.\\\" A player should never have to guess whether a thing is possible.\\n\\n**Flow.** Intro Card (name, one sentence, what you can and can't do, one diagram, this device's prompts; Use to begin)\")\n# section 20\nsub(\"Tippy Raft, plus Step Class and Plate Spinners as logic, and the Check-In.\",\"Step Class on the real balance core, Tippy Raft, Plate Spinners from a moving stick vector, and the Check-In.\")\nsub(\"This overturned my first numbers for Plate Spinners, Tug of Peace, Log Reps, Plank & Perch, Room Service, Tippy Raft, Lean Match, The Cairn's top tier and the keyboard model.\",\"This overturned my first numbers for Plate Spinners, Tug of Peace, Log Reps, Plank & Perch, Room Service, Tippy Raft, Lean Match, The Cairn's top tier, Step Class's lean notes and the keyboard model.\")\n# section 22 counts\nsub(\"*How many issues did testing catch?* About 38 across\",\"*How many issues did testing catch?* About 39 across\")\nsub('\"About 38 across the prototypes and simulations.\"','\"About 39 across the prototypes and simulations.\"')\nopen(p,'w',encoding='utf-8').write(s)\nEOF\ncat > _scratch/clause_audit.py <<'PYEOF'\n# Clause-by-clause: every requirement clause of TASK.md, paired by hand with the plan instruction that answers it.\n# The script only proves the quote is really in that section; the pairing is the reading.\nimport re, sys\nplan=open('PLAN.md',encoding='utf-8').read()\nparts=re.split(r'^## (\\d+)\\. ',plan,flags=re.M); secs={int(parts[i]):parts[i+1] for i in range(1,len(parts),2)}\nclauses={int(a):(b,c) for a,b,c in (l.split('\\t',2) for l in open('_scratch/clauses.txt',encoding='utf-8').read().splitlines())}\nA={\n 2:(1,\"**pitch\"),\n}\nM=[\n (2,1,\"What makes the source itself\"),\n (4,1,\"**Genre:** physics-balance party sports\"),\n (6,1,\"**Perspective:** third person\"),\n (8,1,\"The title is a joke on the source's name, never the name itself\"),\n (9,1,\"Do TASK.md's title step first\"),\n (11,19,\"How much more to research is your choice\"),\n (13,16,\"One self-contained HTML with no external requests\"),\n (14,16,\"this plan inlines everything instead\"),\n (16,16,\"`three@0.180.0`\"),(16,16,\"new THREE.WebGPURenderer\"),(16,9,\"Everything solid is cel-shaded\"),(16,9,\"The ink recipe\"),(16,4,\"RAPIER.JointData.spherical\"),(16,11,\"Everything is synthesised with Web Audio\"),(16,3,\"Left stick, axes 0 and 1\"),\n (17,16,\"`esbuild`, `playwright@1.63.0`, `@fontsource/fredoka`\"),\n (19,9,\"the base is its own toolkit: node materials, lights, shadows and TSL post-processing\"),\n (20,9,\"is a new asset made in code\"),(20,9,\"with its built-in geometries and addons for generic props\"),\n (22,10,\"Use Three's `AnimationMixer` and `AnimationClip` as the base\"),\n (23,10,\"**Doll clips:** idle, breathe, walk\"),\n (25,11,\"Everything is synthesised with Web Audio. No files.\"),\n (26,11,\"Animalese-style gibberish\"),(26,11,\"nonsense Simlish\"),\n (27,11,\"**Music defaults to 10** (gain 0.10)\"),\n (28,12,\"AI Hub session: ghost mode\"),\n (30,16,\"Keep all your dev files in the subfolder TASK.md names\"),\n (31,16,\"bundle them into the single HTML file in the root\"),\n (32,16,\"TASK.md allows external CDN dependencies\"),\n (33,17,\"Don't read the folders beside yours\"),\n (34,17,\"Other agents run here at the same time\"),\n (35,17,\"Prefer `file://`: every test except `hub` opens the built file directly\"),\n (36,17,\"bound to 127.0.0.1 on a port the OS picks, and you confirm the page is your game before trusting a result\"),\n (37,17,\"Stop only processes you started, by their PID. Never `pkill`, `killall`, `fuser -k`, or kill whatever holds a port\"),\n (39,9,\"The performance budget is unlimited\"),\n (40,9,\"Fill the sets: lots of guests, loose props, toy trees, bunting, particles, extra lights\"),\n (42,9,\"FPS targets and optimisation are out of scope\"),\n (44,17,\"scripts that play the game and check its state, including a scripted playthrough of the whole game\"),(44,17,\"**the scripted whole-game playthrough.**\"),\n (45,17,\"one command that prints only failures and a one-line count; rerun it only after changing the code it covers\"),\n (46,17,\"screenshots only for what a script can't check\"),\n (47,17,\"no subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit\"),\n (49,18,\"Each milestone ends with something playable\"),\n (55,17,\"A headed browser needs `xvfb-run`\"),\n (56,17,\"this plan's tools are all Node\"),\n (57,17,\"Do not use TASK.md's three WebGPU flags alone\"),(57,17,\"const RENDER =\"),\n (58,17,\"Pixel 7, iPhone, iPad\"),\n (59,17,\"WebGPU only works on a secure page, `file://` or `http://127.0.0.1`\"),\n (60,17,\"**To see the game\" if False else \"Every test that renders must assert `render.lost` is null\"),\n (61,17,\"`npm i playwright@1.63.0` finds them\"),\n (62,17,\"`PLAYWRIGHT_HOST_PLATFORM_OVERRIDE` is already set\"),\n (67,17,\"means memory ran out, not a bug\"),\n (68,17,\"run fewer browsers rather than retrying\"),\n (71,20,\"\\\"is checked as far as it can be here, never required\\\"\"),\n (72,17,\"Replace `navigator.getGamepads`\"),\n (73,17,\"tapping with `page.touchscreen`\"),\n (74,17,\"`OfflineAudioContext` renders and `AnalyserNode` levels\"),\n (75,17,\"TASK.md suggests two browser pages\"),\n (76,17,\"WebKit with an iPhone profile; it isn't iOS Safari\"),\n (77,17,\"Judge the 10-foot view from screenshots at 1920×1080\"),\n (79,17,\"Other agents run here at the same time\"),\n (80,17,\"Keep to one or two browsers at once and close them when done\"),\n (81,17,\"Keep every file inside your own folder, not `/tmp` (it's shared) or a parent folder\"),\n (82,17,\"Don't run `playwright install` or `playwright install-deps`\"),\n (84,17,\"If you want a Python tool, use `uv run --with ...`\"),\n (87,2,\"This is an original game in the source's genre\"),\n (89,1,\"A feature-complete demo\"),\n (90,1,\"What makes the source itself\"),(90,8,\"**Writing style.**\"),\n (91,1,\"long enough to show everything the game can do\"),(91,6,\"say what you can do here and, in one line, what you can't\"),\n (92,1,\"a complete, polished vertical slice\"),\n (93,14,\"TASK.md wants the rest of the game buildable with normal designer tools\"),\n (94,14,\"From the Pause menu.\"),(94,14,\"**Tools:** jump to any event and tier\"),\n (95,14,\"**Live sliders with Reset to Defaults**\"),\n (97,13,\"After 10 s with no input on the Title or Main menu, start a loop of bot-played vignettes\"),(97,13,\"**Any input exits and is swallowed:**\"),\n (98,13,\"god mode on\"),(98,13,\"let the bots cheat\"),\n (99,13,\"Show as much as possible\"),\n (101,12,\"**Two modes, both required.**\"),(101,12,\"AI Hub session: ghost mode\"),(101,12,\"Group Class: on its own\"),\n (103,8,\"**Writing style.** Short sentences. Polite. Second person.\"),\n (105,3,\"Design for a PS5 DualSense, or any pad the browser reports with `mapping === 'standard'`, on a TV at 10 feet\"),\n (106,3,\"Keyboard and mouse play the same game on the same screens, with no separate desktop layout, and they should feel native rather than like stand-ins\"),\n (107,3,\"W A S D or arrow keys\"),(107,3,\"Left Shift\"),(107,3,\"Esc or Backspace\"),\n (108,3,\"Pointer's offset from screen centre\"),(108,3,\"Hold right button and drag\"),(108,3,\"Left click walks there and uses it\"),(108,3,\"Hover moves the focus\"),(108,3,\"**Hover means the pointer moved\"),\n (109,3,\"**Prompts follow the last input.**\"),\n (110,3,\"PlayStation shapes and Xbox letters (A B X Y\"),(110,3,\"Keyboard prompts show keycaps, mouse prompts show a mouse with the button lit\"),\n (111,7,\"No tables, no scrolling lists of data\"),\n (112,15,\"\\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\" and a Settings button\"),(112,15,\"There are no touch controls anywhere else\"),\n (113,15,\"Attract mode runs after 10 s as usual\"),\n (115,19,\"no TODOs, placeholders or stubbed features\"),\n (116,19,\"the demo is complete\"),\n (119,19,\"go in **your chat reply** and an **in-game About/Credits screen,**\"),\n (120,19,\"Write \\\"unknown\\\" for anything you can't confirm\"),\n (121,19,\"| Date | The date line in your TASK.md |\"),\n (122,19,\"| Source | Wii Fit |\"),\n (123,19,\"| Plan | The file name of the plan you were given |\"),\n (124,19,\"| Genre and Perspective |\"),\n (125,19,\"| Tech | Three.js R180\"),\n (126,19,\"| Art Direction |\"),\n (127,19,\"| Animation |\"),\n (128,19,\"| Audio |\"),\n (129,19,\"| Online |\"),\n (130,19,\"| Testing | The parameters TASK.md allows\"),\n (131,19,\"| Research | Yours, or none\"),\n (132,19,\"| Environment | As written in your TASK.md |\"),\n (135,19,\"| Model | As written in your TASK.md |\"),\n (137,19,\"| Usage | Exactly `added on import`\"),\n (138,19,\"You can't see your own cost, so don't estimate it\"),\n (139,19,\"**the exit-interview file** beside the HTML\"),(139,19,\"one JSON object in TASK.md's exact shape\"),\n (140,19,\"plain text, every value filled in, and you check that it parses\"),\n (142,22,'\"sourceInformation\"'),(158,22,'\"testingFeedback\"'),(160,22,'\"engineFeedback\"'),(162,22,'\"promptFeedback\"'),(164,22,'\"aiHub\"'),\n (166,19,\"| `name` | The game's title, as on its title screen |\"),(168,19,\"| `tagline` |\"),(170,19,\"| `description` |\"),(172,19,\"| `type` | Game |\"),(174,19,\"| `genre` | Sports |\"),(175,19,\"| `source` | Wii Fit |\"),(180,19,\"| `series` | Empty\"),(182,19,\"| `players` | 1–4 |\"),(184,19,\"| `controls` |\"),(186,19,\"| `tags` | 3 to 6 lowercase\"),\n (191,19,\"How many issues did testing catch?\"),(192,19,\"How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking?\"),(193,19,\"What was the most helpful test you ran?\"),(194,19,\"What was the least helpful test you ran?\"),\n (196,19,\"What did you like most about the engine?\"),(197,19,\"Did you get stuck or guess wrong?\"),(198,19,\"What was the most important thing you had to build yourself?\"),(199,19,\"What was the hardest part about using the engine?\"),(200,19,\"What did you change in the engine, and why? (none if nothing)\"),\n]\n# clauses with no requirement in them, each with the reason\nINFO={1:'heading',3:'heading',5:'heading',7:'heading',10:'heading',12:'heading',15:'heading',18:'heading',21:'heading',24:'heading',29:'heading',38:'heading',41:'heading',43:'heading',48:'heading',50:'heading',51:'when the check ran',52:'machine facts',53:'machine facts',54:'disk facts; the /tmp rule is clause 81',63:'tool versions',64:'tool versions',65:'not installed; nothing depends on them',66:'network works',69:'heading',70:'context for clause 71',78:'heading',83:'context for clause 84',85:'context for clause 84',86:'heading',88:'heading',96:'heading',100:'heading',102:'heading',104:'heading',114:'heading',117:'heading',118:'heading',133:'value of clause 132',134:'value of clause 132',136:'value of clause 135',141:'JSON syntax',187:'JSON syntax',188:'JSON syntax',189:'says these are not asked',190:'heading',195:'heading'}\nfor n in list(clauses):\n    b,c=clauses[n]\n    if re.fullmatch(r'\"[a-zA-Z]+\":|\"\", \"[a-zA-Z]+\":|\"added on import\"\\},|\\[\"your answer.*\\],?|\"the game\\'s title.*|\"a few words.*|\"one or two sentences.*|\"Game, Tech demo.*|\"one of Action.*|\"the work it\\'s based on, e\\.g\\.|Moby-Dick\",|\"its franchise, e\\.g\\.|Star Fox, or empty\",|\"how many can play.*|\"the controls, in one line\",|\\[\"3 to 6 lowercase.*|\"sourceInformation\": \\{\"date\":|\"aiHub\": \\{',c): INFO.setdefault(n,'part of the JSON shape; checked key by key below')\nfails=[];paired={}\nfor n,sec,q in M:\n    if q not in secs[sec]: fails.append(f'clause {n}: not in section {sec}: {q[:70]}')\n    paired.setdefault(n,[]).append((sec,q))\n# remaining feedback questions past the listing\nrest=[n for n in clauses if n not in paired and n not in INFO]\nfor n in rest:\n    c=clauses[n][1].lstrip('- ').strip()\n    if c.endswith('?') or c.endswith('(none if nothing)'):\n        if c in secs[19]: paired[n]=[(19,c)]\n        else: fails.append(f'clause {n}: question missing: {c}')\n    else: fails.append(f'clause {n}: UNANSWERED: {c[:110]}')\nprint(f'{len(clauses)} clauses: {len(paired)} requirements paired with an instruction, {len([n for n in clauses if n in INFO and n not in paired])} carry no requirement')\nfor f in fails: print('FAIL',f)\nif '--show' in sys.argv:\n    for n in sorted(paired):\n        print(f'[{n}] {clauses[n][1][:92]}')\n        for sec,q in paired[n][:2]: print(f'     §{sec}: {q[:104]}')\nPYEOF\npython3 _scratch/clause_audit.py","description":"Fix plan gaps and pair every TASK.md clause with its instruction"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8406,"cache_read_input_tokens":806458,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8406},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"19307802-7215-43fb-a84b-6c94bbc636c5","uuid":"f9c3d8fe-f572-4742-b5b5-8500ae22dbd4","timestamp":"2026-11-05T06:09:23.453Z","request_id":"req_011CgjHGHSFRkQP1eJS6UHgL","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01Y5DWZXtE5CMtKHEuxgNCM7":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211905__xe6f2a4/work && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='PLAN.md'\ns=open(p,encoding='utf-8').read()\ndef sub(old,new):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(old)==1, ('COUNT %d: '%s.count(old))+old[:90]\n    s=s.replace(old,new)\n# Step Class\nsub(\"- *Windows (starting values):* Perfect ±45 ms, Good ±90, OK ±135.\",\"- *Windows ✔:* Perfect ±45 ms, Good ±90, OK ±135 for feet.\")\nsub(\"Session version: 24 bars at 116.\",\"Session version: 24 bars at 116, with a 4-bar lean break.\")\na=s.index(\"- *Scoring ✔:* Perfect 1, Good .7, OK .4; form is the share of the maximum.\")\nb=s.index(\"- *Bot:* hits every note with its skill's timing error.\")\ns=s[:a]+\"\"\"- *Lean notes are judged differently ✔.* A soft-bodied doll physically can't get its dot across in one beat: in Tier 1's break, which swings end to end, it takes .6-.9 s against a .58 s beat, so even a perfect player would be marked late. A lean note scores when the dot passes .25 in that direction: full marks within 1.5 beats, half within 2. The ribbon scrolls toward you, so players can lead it with the stick.\n- *Scoring ✔ (whole run on the real balance core):* feet Perfect 1, Good .7, OK .4; form is the share of the maximum. With timing error sd 28 / 55 / 95 ms and a small miss rate: Tier 1 97 / 84 / 62, Tier 2 97 / 85 / 64, Tier 3 97 / 84 / 63, with lean notes at 100 / 97 / 67, 100 / 100 / 88 and 100 / 96 / 84. The tiers have 106 notes in 102 s, 108 in 91 s and 126 in 85 s, with no falls (peak lean 24-26°). The session version takes 49.7 s, with 54 foot and 10 lean notes, and fits its 50 s slot: 98 / 88 / 69.\n\"\"\"+s[b:]\n# Plate Spinners\nsub(\"- *Measure:* hoop ω = smoothed angular velocity of the weight vector when |weight| > 0.5; otherwise it decays.\",\"- *Measure:* hoop ω = angular velocity of the weight vector when |weight| > 0.5, smoothed with τ = .12 s; otherwise it decays at 3 /s.\")\nsub(\"- *Tiers ✔, 60 s:* start energy .7, gain .45 per s. Tier 1: L M S, decay .11. Tier 2: L M M S, decay .13. Tier 3: L L M M S S, decay .16. Share of plate-time alive: Tier 1 100% / 87% / 73%, Tier 2 90 / 80 / 67, Tier 3 79 / 70 / 61. Crashes a minute: 0 / 4 / 8 on Tier 1, more above.\",\n    \"- *Tiers ✔, 60 s:* start energy .7, gain .45 per s. Tier 1: L M S, decay .11. Tier 2: L M M S, decay .13. Tier 3: L L M M S S, decay .16. Share of plate-time alive, from a simulated stick moving in a circle with hand jitter, rate wander and slips, measured as above: Tier 1 100% / 89% / 82%, Tier 2 89 / 86 / 74, Tier 3 79 / 76 / 66. Crashes a minute: 0 / 3.5 / 6 on Tier 1, more above. The smoothing isn't critical (.05 to .25 s gives much the same).\")\nsub(\"- *Scoring:* form = `200 × share − 100`, floored at 0 ✔ Tier 1 100 / 74 / 46.\",\"- *Scoring:* form = `200 × share − 100`, floored at 0 ✔ Tier 1 100 / 78 / 64.\")\n# clause 30, 31\nsub(\"**Stack.** `three@0.180.0`\",\"**Where things go.** Keep all your dev files in the subfolder TASK.md names (your dev folder). Develop separate modules there, and bundle them into the single HTML file in the root, named as TASK.md says, when you're done. TASK.md allows external CDN dependencies; this plan inlines everything instead, so the file works offline and inside the hub.\\n\\n**Stack.** `three@0.180.0`\")\n# clause 75\nsub(\"| Second player | The harness's 2-4 copies for sessions, four stubbed pads for Group Class |\",\"| Second player | TASK.md suggests two browser pages. The hub's harness is that test, built for this: it plays 2-4 copies at once, in frames of one page, on a simulated network. Add four stubbed pads for Group Class |\")\n# clause 91\nsub(\"**Flow.** Intro Card (name, one sentence, one diagram, this device's prompts; Use to begin)\",\"**What you can and can't do.** Every Intro Card and the How to Play page say what you can do here and, in one line, what you can't: \\\"You can't fall in this one.\\\" \\\"Your feet don't matter here.\\\" \\\"You can't lose this; you can only do it badly.\\\" A player should never have to guess whether a thing is possible.\\n\\n**Flow.** Intro Card (name, one sentence, what you can and can't do, one diagram, this device's prompts; Use to begin)\")\n# section 20\nsub(\"Tippy Raft, plus Step Class and Plate Spinners as logic, and the Check-In.\",\"Step Class on the real balance core, Tippy Raft, Plate Spinners from a moving stick vector, and the Check-In.\")\nsub(\"This overturned my first numbers for Plate Spinners, Tug of Peace, Log Reps, Plank & Perch, Room Service, Tippy Raft, Lean Match, The Cairn's top tier and the keyboard model.\",\"This overturned my first numbers for Plate Spinners, Tug of Peace, Log Reps, Plank & Perch, Room Service, Tippy Raft, Lean Match, The Cairn's top tier, Step Class's lean notes and the keyboard model.\")\n# section 22 counts\nsub(\"*How many issues did testing catch?* About 38 across\",\"*How many issues did testing catch?* About 39 across\")\nsub('\"About 38 across the prototypes and simulations.\"','\"About 39 across the prototypes and simulations.\"')\nopen(p,'w',encoding='utf-8').write(s)\nEOF\ncat > _scratch/clause_audit.py <<'PYEOF'\n# Clause-by-clause: every requirement clause of TASK.md, paired by hand with the plan instruction that answers it.\n# The script only proves the quote is really in that section; the pairing is the reading.\nimport re, sys\nplan=open('PLAN.md',encoding='utf-8').read()\nparts=re.split(r'^## (\\d+)\\. ',plan,flags=re.M); secs={int(parts[i]):parts[i+1] for i in range(1,len(parts),2)}\nclauses={int(a):(b,c) for a,b,c in (l.split('\\t',2) for l in open('_scratch/clauses.txt',encoding='utf-8').read().splitlines())}\nA={\n 2:(1,\"**pitch\"),\n}\nM=[\n (2,1,\"What makes the source itself\"),\n (4,1,\"**Genre:** physics-balance party sports\"),\n (6,1,\"**Perspective:** third person\"),\n (8,1,\"The title is a joke on the source's name, never the name itself\"),\n (9,1,\"Do TASK.md's title step first\"),\n (11,19,\"How much more to research is your choice\"),\n (13,16,\"One self-contained HTML with no external requests\"),\n (14,16,\"this plan inlines everything instead\"),\n (16,16,\"`three@0.180.0`\"),(16,16,\"new THREE.WebGPURenderer\"),(16,9,\"Everything solid is cel-shaded\"),(16,9,\"The ink recipe\"),(16,4,\"RAPIER.JointData.spherical\"),(16,11,\"Everything is synthesised with Web Audio\"),(16,3,\"Left stick, axes 0 and 1\"),\n (17,16,\"`esbuild`, `playwright@1.63.0`, `@fontsource/fredoka`\"),\n (19,9,\"the base is its own toolkit: node materials, lights, shadows and TSL post-processing\"),\n (20,9,\"is a new asset made in code\"),(20,9,\"with its built-in geometries and addons for generic props\"),\n (22,10,\"Use Three's `AnimationMixer` and `AnimationClip` as the base\"),\n (23,10,\"**Doll clips:** idle, breathe, walk\"),\n (25,11,\"Everything is synthesised with Web Audio. No files.\"),\n (26,11,\"Animalese-style gibberish\"),(26,11,\"nonsense Simlish\"),\n (27,11,\"**Music defaults to 10** (gain 0.10)\"),\n (28,12,\"AI Hub session: ghost mode\"),\n (30,16,\"Keep all your dev files in the subfolder TASK.md names\"),\n (31,16,\"bundle them into the single HTML file in the root\"),\n (32,16,\"TASK.md allows external CDN dependencies\"),\n (33,17,\"Don't read the folders beside yours\"),\n (34,17,\"Other agents run here at the same time\"),\n (35,17,\"Prefer `file://`: every test except `hub` opens the built file directly\"),\n (36,17,\"bound to 127.0.0.1 on a port the OS picks, and you confirm the page is your game before trusting a result\"),\n (37,17,\"Stop only processes you started, by their PID. Never `pkill`, `killall`, `fuser -k`, or kill whatever holds a port\"),\n (39,9,\"The performance budget is unlimited\"),\n (40,9,\"Fill the sets: lots of guests, loose props, toy trees, bunting, particles, extra lights\"),\n (42,9,\"FPS targets and optimisation are out of scope\"),\n (44,17,\"scripts that play the game and check its state, including a scripted playthrough of the whole game\"),(44,17,\"**the scripted whole-game playthrough.**\"),\n (45,17,\"one command that prints only failures and a one-line count; rerun it only after changing the code it covers\"),\n (46,17,\"screenshots only for what a script can't check\"),\n (47,17,\"no subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit\"),\n (49,18,\"Each milestone ends with something playable\"),\n (55,17,\"A headed browser needs `xvfb-run`\"),\n (56,17,\"this plan's tools are all Node\"),\n (57,17,\"Do not use TASK.md's three WebGPU flags alone\"),(57,17,\"const RENDER =\"),\n (58,17,\"Pixel 7, iPhone, iPad\"),\n (59,17,\"WebGPU only works on a secure page, `file://` or `http://127.0.0.1`\"),\n (60,17,\"**To see the game\" if False else \"Every test that renders must assert `render.lost` is null\"),\n (61,17,\"`npm i playwright@1.63.0` finds them\"),\n (62,17,\"`PLAYWRIGHT_HOST_PLATFORM_OVERRIDE` is already set\"),\n (67,17,\"means memory ran out, not a bug\"),\n (68,17,\"run fewer browsers rather than retrying\"),\n (71,20,\"\\\"is checked as far as it can be here, never required\\\"\"),\n (72,17,\"Replace `navigator.getGamepads`\"),\n (73,17,\"tapping with `page.touchscreen`\"),\n (74,17,\"`OfflineAudioContext` renders and `AnalyserNode` levels\"),\n (75,17,\"TASK.md suggests two browser pages\"),\n (76,17,\"WebKit with an iPhone profile; it isn't iOS Safari\"),\n (77,17,\"Judge the 10-foot view from screenshots at 1920×1080\"),\n (79,17,\"Other agents run here at the same time\"),\n (80,17,\"Keep to one or two browsers at once and close them when done\"),\n (81,17,\"Keep every file inside your own folder, not `/tmp` (it's shared) or a parent folder\"),\n (82,17,\"Don't run `playwright install` or `playwright install-deps`\"),\n (84,17,\"If you want a Python tool, use `uv run --with ...`\"),\n (87,2,\"This is an original game in the source's genre\"),\n (89,1,\"A feature-complete demo\"),\n (90,1,\"What makes the source itself\"),(90,8,\"**Writing style.**\"),\n (91,1,\"long enough to show everything the game can do\"),(91,6,\"say what you can do here and, in one line, what you can't\"),\n (92,1,\"a complete, polished vertical slice\"),\n (93,14,\"TASK.md wants the rest of the game buildable with normal designer tools\"),\n (94,14,\"From the Pause menu.\"),(94,14,\"**Tools:** jump to any event and tier\"),\n (95,14,\"**Live sliders with Reset to Defaults**\"),\n (97,13,\"After 10 s with no input on the Title or Main menu, start a loop of bot-played vignettes\"),(97,13,\"**Any input exits and is swallowed:**\"),\n (98,13,\"god mode on\"),(98,13,\"let the bots cheat\"),\n (99,13,\"Show as much as possible\"),\n (101,12,\"**Two modes, both required.**\"),(101,12,\"AI Hub session: ghost mode\"),(101,12,\"Group Class: on its own\"),\n (103,8,\"**Writing style.** Short sentences. Polite. Second person.\"),\n (105,3,\"Design for a PS5 DualSense, or any pad the browser reports with `mapping === 'standard'`, on a TV at 10 feet\"),\n (106,3,\"Keyboard and mouse play the same game on the same screens, with no separate desktop layout, and they should feel native rather than like stand-ins\"),\n (107,3,\"W A S D or arrow keys\"),(107,3,\"Left Shift\"),(107,3,\"Esc or Backspace\"),\n (108,3,\"Pointer's offset from screen centre\"),(108,3,\"Hold right button and drag\"),(108,3,\"Left click walks there and uses it\"),(108,3,\"Hover moves the focus\"),(108,3,\"**Hover means the pointer moved\"),\n (109,3,\"**Prompts follow the last input.**\"),\n (110,3,\"PlayStation shapes and Xbox letters (A B X Y\"),(110,3,\"Keyboard prompts show keycaps, mouse prompts show a mouse with the button lit\"),\n (111,7,\"No tables, no scrolling lists of data\"),\n (112,15,\"\\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\" and a Settings button\"),(112,15,\"There are no touch controls anywhere else\"),\n (113,15,\"Attract mode runs after 10 s as usual\"),\n (115,19,\"no TODOs, placeholders or stubbed features\"),\n (116,19,\"the demo is complete\"),\n (119,19,\"go in **your chat reply** and an **in-game About/Credits screen,**\"),\n (120,19,\"Write \\\"unknown\\\" for anything you can't confirm\"),\n (121,19,\"| Date | The date line in your TASK.md |\"),\n (122,19,\"| Source | Wii Fit |\"),\n (123,19,\"| Plan | The file name of the plan you were given |\"),\n (124,19,\"| Genre and Perspective |\"),\n (125,19,\"| Tech | Three.js R180\"),\n (126,19,\"| Art Direction |\"),\n (127,19,\"| Animation |\"),\n (128,19,\"| Audio |\"),\n (129,19,\"| Online |\"),\n (130,19,\"| Testing | The parameters TASK.md allows\"),\n (131,19,\"| Research | Yours, or none\"),\n (132,19,\"| Environment | As written in your TASK.md |\"),\n (135,19,\"| Model | As written in your TASK.md |\"),\n (137,19,\"| Usage | Exactly `added on import`\"),\n (138,19,\"You can't see your own cost, so don't estimate it\"),\n (139,19,\"**the exit-interview file** beside the HTML\"),(139,19,\"one JSON object in TASK.md's exact shape\"),\n (140,19,\"plain text, every value filled in, and you check that it parses\"),\n (142,22,'\"sourceInformation\"'),(158,22,'\"testingFeedback\"'),(160,22,'\"engineFeedback\"'),(162,22,'\"promptFeedback\"'),(164,22,'\"aiHub\"'),\n (166,19,\"| `name` | The game's title, as on its title screen |\"),(168,19,\"| `tagline` |\"),(170,19,\"| `description` |\"),(172,19,\"| `type` | Game |\"),(174,19,\"| `genre` | Sports |\"),(175,19,\"| `source` | Wii Fit |\"),(180,19,\"| `series` | Empty\"),(182,19,\"| `players` | 1–4 |\"),(184,19,\"| `controls` |\"),(186,19,\"| `tags` | 3 to 6 lowercase\"),\n (191,19,\"How many issues did testing catch?\"),(192,19,\"How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking?\"),(193,19,\"What was the most helpful test you ran?\"),(194,19,\"What was the least helpful test you ran?\"),\n (196,19,\"What did you like most about the engine?\"),(197,19,\"Did you get stuck or guess wrong?\"),(198,19,\"What was the most important thing you had to build yourself?\"),(199,19,\"What was the hardest part about using the engine?\"),(200,19,\"What did you change in the engine, and why? (none if nothing)\"),\n]\n# clauses with no requirement in them, each with the reason\nINFO={1:'heading',3:'heading',5:'heading',7:'heading',10:'heading',12:'heading',15:'heading',18:'heading',21:'heading',24:'heading',29:'heading',38:'heading',41:'heading',43:'heading',48:'heading',50:'heading',51:'when the check ran',52:'machine facts',53:'machine facts',54:'disk facts; the /tmp rule is clause 81',63:'tool versions',64:'tool versions',65:'not installed; nothing depends on them',66:'network works',69:'heading',70:'context for clause 71',78:'heading',83:'context for clause 84',85:'context for clause 84',86:'heading',88:'heading',96:'heading',100:'heading',102:'heading',104:'heading',114:'heading',117:'heading',118:'heading',133:'value of clause 132',134:'value of clause 132',136:'value of clause 135',141:'JSON syntax',187:'JSON syntax',188:'JSON syntax',189:'says these are not asked',190:'heading',195:'heading'}\nfor n in list(clauses):\n    b,c=clauses[n]\n    if re.fullmatch(r'\"[a-zA-Z]+\":|\"\", \"[a-zA-Z]+\":|\"added on import\"\\},|\\[\"your answer.*\\],?|\"the game\\'s title.*|\"a few words.*|\"one or two sentences.*|\"Game, Tech demo.*|\"one of Action.*|\"the work it\\'s based on, e\\.g\\.|Moby-Dick\",|\"its franchise, e\\.g\\.|Star Fox, or empty\",|\"how many can play.*|\"the controls, in one line\",|\\[\"3 to 6 lowercase.*|\"sourceInformation\": \\{\"date\":|\"aiHub\": \\{',c): INFO.setdefault(n,'part of the JSON shape; checked key by key below')\nfails=[];paired={}\nfor n,sec,q in M:\n    if q not in secs[sec]: fails.append(f'clause {n}: not in section {sec}: {q[:70]}')\n    paired.setdefault(n,[]).append((sec,q))\n# remaining feedback questions past the listing\nrest=[n for n in clauses if n not in paired and n not in INFO]\nfor n in rest:\n    c=clauses[n][1].lstrip('- ').strip()\n    if c.endswith('?') or c.endswith('(none if nothing)'):\n        if c in secs[19]: paired[n]=[(19,c)]\n        else: fails.append(f'clause {n}: question missing: {c}')\n    else: fails.append(f'clause {n}: UNANSWERED: {c[:110]}')\nprint(f'{len(clauses)} clauses: {len(paired)} requirements paired with an instruction, {len([n for n in clauses if n in INFO and n not in paired])} carry no requirement')\nfor f in fails: print('FAIL',f)\nif '--show' in sys.argv:\n    for n in sorted(paired):\n        print(f'[{n}] {clauses[n][1][:92]}')\n        for sec,q in paired[n][:2]: print(f'     §{sec}: {q[:104]}')\nPYEOF\npython3 _scratch/clause_audit.py","description":"Fix plan gaps and pair every TASK.md clause with its instruction"}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_01Y5DWZXtE5CMtKHEuxgNCM7":{"cwd":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211905__xe6f2a4/work"}}}
