{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjHQ52MKhVb6VDnEZD7j","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`PLAN.md` covers everything `TASK.md` asks for, and this time I checked that by reading it clause by clause rather than matching phrases. Two of the hook's remaining objections can't be met at this stage, and I explain why below rather than faking them.\n\n## What I closed\n- **Clause-by-clause audit:** I split `TASK.md` into its 206 clauses. 78 carry no requirement (headings, machine facts), and I paired the other 128 by hand with the instruction that answers them, then read every pair. The script only confirmed each quote really exists in that section; the judgement is mine.\n- **Three gaps that audit found, now fixed:**\n  - Clause 30: keeping dev files in the named subfolder was only implied.\n  - Clause 75: \"two browser pages\" was silently swapped for the harness. The plan now says so and explains why.\n  - Clause 91: nothing covered what a player \"cannot do\". Every Intro Card and the How to Play page now say it.\n- **Simulations:** Step Class and Plate Spinners are no longer logic-only.\n  - **Step Class** on the real balance core found a real flaw: the doll can't get its dot across in one beat, so even a perfect player was marked late. Lean notes now have their own rule, and scores are 97 / 84 / 62 (sharp / average / clumsy bots) on Tier 1.\n  - **Plate Spinners** from a simulated noisy stick held up, at 100% / 89% / 82% of plate-time kept alive.\n\nEvery event now has simulated numbers. These are still simulations of a player, and only Fruit Hat was built into the integration prototype.\n\n## What I can't do\n- **A build's own About screen, exit file and reporting:** `STAGE.md` says other agents build the game \"without you\", so no build exists for these to describe. Writing them now would be false reporting, and an `exit-interview.json` here could end up in the run's records. Section 19 tells builders exactly what to write, section 22 shows the exact shape, and the prototype proved the About screen shows every field from that file.\n- **Hearing the audio, or playing on a real controller and TV:** these aren't available here. `TASK.md` itself says such things are \"checked as far as it can be here, never required\". Audio was checked as signals, input through stubs, and the 10-foot view through 1920×1080 screenshots.\n\nIf the hook keeps blocking only on these two, more work won't clear it, because they can't be satisfied before a build exists. `/goal clear` would end it.\n\n## Reporting from the planning stage\nThis is also in section 22. Builders report on their own builds.\n\n**Source Information**\n- **Date:** 2026-11-04 21:19:05\n- **Source:** Wii Fit\n- **Plan:** none\n- **Genre and Perspective:** physics-balance party sports with a daily-ritual progression; third person, with framed stage cameras and an orbitable chase camera\n- **Tech:** Three.js R180 (WebGPU, WebGL2 fallback), Rapier 0.19.3, Web Audio, Gamepad API, esbuild 0.28.2, Playwright 1.63.0, Fredoka 5.3.0\n- **Art Direction:** cel-shaded ink over a wooden-toy resort, all models made in code\n- **Animation:** `AnimationMixer` clips on jointed rigs, physics-driven lean, Rapier ragdolls (prototyped with test clips)\n- **Audio:** code-synthesised city-pop and bossa at 10% by default, effects, Animalese and Simlish-style voices (only the title theme, voices and foot click prototyped)\n- **Online:** AI Hub Session Protocol v1 in ghost mode for 1–4 devices, plus 1–4 on one screen\n- **Testing:** as much headless testing as wanted, using scripts that play the game and check state, including a whole-game playthrough; one command printing only failures and a one-line count, rerun only after code changes; screenshots only for what a script can't check; no subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit\n- **Research:** hub protocol pages and code; source background from search summaries\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort max\n- **Usage:** added on import\n\n**Testing Feedback**\n1. **Issues caught:** about 39.\n2. **Critical:** 13, listed in section 22.\n3. **Most helpful:** building one event through everything from the plan's own recipes.\n4. **Least helpful:** the Firefox WebGL2 checks, which changed nothing in the game.\n\n**Engine Feedback**\n1. **Liked most:** `toonOutlinePass` plus a short TSL pass gave the whole ink look, unchanged on WebGPU and WebGL2.\n2. **Stuck or guessed wrong:** yes. I took a lost device for 60 fps, and convex-hull stones collapsed on their own.\n3. **Most important thing built:** the balance core, a torque-limited controller on a ball joint.\n4. **Hardest part:** knowing what was really happening. A lost device gives no JavaScript error and the loop keeps running, and a Rapier crash can surface half a second after its cause.\n5. **Changed in the engine:** none.\n6. **One change:** make Rapier's panic a catchable error.\n\n**Prompt Feedback**\n1. **Liked most:** open creative choices combined with exact, checkable facts.\n2. **Confusing:** what \"the game on its own\" means for multiplayer, \"native style\" for an engine with none, and which parts of `TASK.md` apply at the plan stage.\n3. **Hardest:** making a balance game a steady thumb can't trivially beat, while staying original.\n4. **Would change:** fix the WebGPU flags, define standalone multiplayer, and state how capable builders are.\n\nNothing is committed, and my scratch files are deleted.\n\n## Files are in the run's `work` folder\n- `PLAN.md`\n- `planner-exit-interview.json`\n\nSources (read as search summaries, not full pages):\n- [Wii Fit, Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wii_Fit)\n- [Iwata Asks: Wii Fit, part 3, page 2](https://iwataasks.nintendo.com/interviews/wii/wii_fit/3/2)\n- [Iwata Asks: Wii Fit, part 3, page 4](https://iwataasks.nintendo.com/interviews/wii/wii_fit/3/4)\n- [Nintendo World Report review](https://nintendoworldreport.com/review/16177/wii-fit-wii)\n- [AI Hub Session Protocol](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/README.md)"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2716,"cache_read_input_tokens":831066,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2716},"output_tokens":694,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"19307802-7215-43fb-a84b-6c94bbc636c5","uuid":"051a50de-7396-4fc1-9567-5e0044878cb1","timestamp":"2026-11-05T06:10:10.092Z","request_id":"req_011CgjHQ4g1y77tMLgaF18KB"}
